 It ships with 12GB of GDDR6X memory, 7168 CUDA cores, and swappable magnetic backplates inspired by the game\'s expansions — bringing together serious 1440p/4K gaming performance and standout collector-grade style.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>Built in collaboration with Blizzard Entertainment, this limited edition graphics card celebrates the 20th anniversary of World of Warcraft and the release of The War Within expansion. It\'s finished in the game\'s signature Mystic Blue and Glorious Gold color scheme, and includes a set of magnetic backplates inspired by WoW\'s ten expansions, which owners can swap out to match their personal style. <a href=\"https://www.alktech.co/articles/review-msi-geforce-rtx-4070-super-12g-gaming-slim-world-of-warcraft-edition\">Alktech + 2</a></p><p>Under the hood, the card runs on NVIDIA\'s GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER GPU with 7168 CUDA cores, 12GB of GDDR6X memory on a 192-bit bus running at 21 Gbps, and boost clocks up to 2475 MHz (2490 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode). That translates to a memory bandwidth of roughly 504 GB/s, giving it plenty of headroom for high-refresh 1440p gaming and demanding 4K workloads. <a href=\"https://www.msi.com/Graphics-Card/GeForce-RTX-4070-SUPER-12G-GAMING-SLIM-World-of-Warcraft-EDITION/Specification\">MSI</a><a href=\"https://www.gpu-monkey.com/en/gpu-msi_geforce_rtx_4070_super_12g_gaming_slim_world_of_warcraft_edition\">GPU Monkey</a></p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen ray tracing, fourth-gen Tensor Cores, and DLSS 3 frame generation for smoother, more responsive gameplay, plus NVIDIA Reflex for reduced input latency. MSI\'s cooling design features TORX Fan 5.0 blades linked by ring arcs with a fan cowl to stabilize and maintain high-pressure airflow, a copper baseplate to capture heat from the GPU and memory, square-shaped core heat pipes for maximum GPU contact, and staggered heatsink fin sections to reduce airflow noise. An illuminated dragon logo adds a signature MSI touch, and the whole card ships in a themed carry case with a WoW 20th-anniversary motif, along with a thank-you card and the full set of expansion backplates. <a href=\"https://shwetacomputers.com/products/msi-geforce-rtx-4070-super-12g-gaming-slim-world-of-warcraft%C2%AE-edition\">Shweta Computers</a><a href=\"https://www.alktech.co/articles/review-msi-geforce-rtx-4070-super-12g-gaming-slim-world-of-warcraft-edition\">Alktech</a></p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER (AD104)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>7168 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>56 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>224 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2475 MHz (up to 2490 MHz in Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>12GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>192-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>21 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~504 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v1.4a), 1x HDMI (2.1a — 4K@120Hz HDR, 8K@60Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4 simultaneous</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Included Adapter</td><td>2x 8-pin to 1x 16-pin adapter cable</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>650W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>TORX Fan 5.0, copper baseplate, square core heat pipes, airflow-control fin design</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Special Edition</td><td>Swappable magnetic backplates (10 WoW expansion designs)</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Lighting</td><td>Illuminated MSI dragon logo</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Dimensions</td><td>307mm x 125mm x 46mm</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 3 (AI frame generation)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center (monitoring, tuning, RGB control)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>Want this formatted into a ready-to-use HTML/Markdown product page file, or fitted to a specific e-commerce platform\'s field structure (Shopify, WooCommerce, Amazon, etc.)?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G GAMING X SLIM GDDR6X Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have solid specs on this variant. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G GAMING X SLIM</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 SUPER 12G Gaming X Slim | 12GB GDDR6X Graphics Card</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Buy the MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G Gaming X Slim — 12GB GDDR6X, 7168 CUDA cores, TRI FROZR 3 cooling, DLSS 3, up to 2640 MHz boost clock. Shop now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 SUPER Gaming X Slim, RTX 4070 Super 12GB, MSI RTX 4070 Super price, TRI FROZR 3 graphics card, 12GB GDDR6X GPU, DLSS 3 graphics card, Ada Lovelace GPU, SFF-ready RTX GPU, RTX 4070 Super specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G Gaming X Slim delivers premium 1440p and 4K gaming performance in a compact, SFF-friendly design. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture with 12GB of GDDR6X memory, 7168 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2640 MHz, it\'s cooled by MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design with triple TORX Fan 5.0 blades — combining strong performance, quiet operation, and a slimmer footprint than standard Gaming X cards.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G Gaming X Slim is built around the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER GPU, offering 7168 CUDA cores — 20% more than the standard RTX 4070 — along with 12GB of GDDR6X memory across a 192-bit bus at 21 Gbps. Boost clocks reach 2640 MHz out of the box, with MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode pushing that to 2655 MHz, giving this card the muscle for high-frame-rate 1440p gaming and demanding 4K workloads alike.</p><p>Powered by NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-generation RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing, fourth-generation Tensor Cores paired with an Optical Flow Accelerator for AI-driven DLSS 3 frame generation, and NVIDIA Reflex to minimize system latency for competitive gaming. As part of the \"Gaming Slim\" line, it\'s designed as a thinner variant of the standard Gaming series while still maintaining high performance and an aggressive look, making it a strong fit for small form factor builds. <a href=\"https://www.msi.com/Graphics-Card/GeForce-RTX-4070-SUPER-12G-GAMING-X-SLIM-MLG\">MSI</a></p><p>Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design, featuring TORX Fan 5.0 blades linked by ring arcs and a fan cowl to stabilize and concentrate airflow, a copper baseplate that pulls heat away from the GPU and memory modules, square-shaped core heat pipes for maximum GPU contact, and Airflow Control fin sections that reduce turbulence and noise. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring and tuning, with MSI Afterburner available for more advanced overclocking control, and MSI Mystic Light for customizable RGB lighting synced with other MSI and compatible third-party components.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER (AD104)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>7168 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>56 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>224 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2640 MHz (up to 2655 MHz in Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>12GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>192-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>21 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~504 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v1.4a), 1x HDMI (2.1a — 4K@120Hz HDR, 8K@60Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320 @ 60Hz</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>~245 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>650W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>TRI FROZR 3 with triple TORX Fan 5.0, copper baseplate, core pipes, Airflow Control</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Form Factor</td><td>Gaming Slim (thinner than standard Gaming series), SFF-ready</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Lighting</td><td>MSI Mystic Light RGB</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 3 (AI frame generation)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center, MSI Afterburner</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>Want this exported as a ready-to-use file (HTML, Markdown, or CSV for a specific e-commerce platform)?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G INSPIRE 3X OC GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have solid data on this one. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G INSPIRE 3X OC</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 12G Inspire 3X OC | 12GB GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Get the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Inspire 3X OC — 12GB GDDR7, Blackwell architecture, DLSS 4, triple STORMFORCE fans, up to 2557 MHz boost. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Inspire 3X OC, RTX 5070 12GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5070 price, Blackwell graphics card, DLSS 4 graphics card, PCIe 5.0 GPU, STORMFORCE fan GPU, SFF-ready graphics card, RTX 5070 specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Inspire 3X OC brings NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and next-gen DLSS 4 to a compact, small-form-factor-friendly design. It features 12GB of GDDR7 memory, 6144 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2557 MHz, cooled by a triple STORMFORCE fan thermal solution — built for creators and gamers who want strong performance without a bulky card.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Inspire 3X OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 GPU, built on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture. It packs 6144 CUDA cores, 12GB of next-gen GDDR7 memory on a 192-bit bus running at 28 Gbps, and a factory-overclocked boost clock of 2542 MHz in Gaming/Silent mode, reaching up to 2557 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode. This marks a generational leap over GDDR6X-based predecessors, delivering higher memory bandwidth for smoother 1440p and 4K gaming.</p><p>Blackwell brings DLSS 4 support to the table, along with updated ray tracing and Tensor Core hardware for AI-accelerated rendering and content creation. Display output has also been upgraded, with DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b connectors supporting resolutions and refresh rates up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, Gaming VRR, and HDR. <a href=\"https://us-store.msi.com/RTX-5070\">MSI</a></p><p>True to its name, the INSPIRE series pairs a small form factor with strong performance, making it a natural fit for compact builds and creative workstations. Cooling comes from a triple-fan design using seven-blade STORMFORCE fans with claw texturing for optimal airflow and reduced noise, paired with a nickel-plated copper baseplate that captures and transfers heat from the GPU and memory, square-profile core pipes for maximum thermal contact, and WAVE-CURVED 3.0 fin optimization to fine-tune airflow efficiency around the fan motor. A metal backplate with vents and thermal pads rounds out the cooling package. The card is managed through MSI Center, which offers both a Gaming mode for maximum performance and a Silent mode for quieter operation, plus MSI Afterburner for advanced overclocking control. <a href=\"https://us-store.msi.com/RTX-5070\">MSI</a><a href=\"https://videocardz.net/msi-geforce-rtx-5070-12gb-inspire-3x-oc\">VideoCardz</a></p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 (GB205-300)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>6144 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2542 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode), up to 2557 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>12GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>192-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>28 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>~250 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>650W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Length</td><td>288 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Slot Size</td><td>Dual-slot</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x STORMFORCE fans</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>Nickel-plated copper baseplate, square core pipes, WAVE-CURVED 3.0, Air Antegrade Fin</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Backplate</td><td>Metal backplate with vents and thermal pads</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Form Factor</td><td>Compact/SFF-ready design</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center (Gaming/Silent mode), MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>Want this exported as a ready-to-use file (HTML, Markdown, or CSV for a specific platform)?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G GAMING TRIO OC WHITE GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have solid data. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G GAMING TRIO OC WHITE</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 12G Gaming Trio OC White | 12GB GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Shop the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Gaming Trio OC White — 12GB GDDR7, TRI FROZR 4 cooling, DLSS 4, up to 2610 MHz boost clock, sleek white design. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Gaming Trio OC White, RTX 5070 white graphics card, RTX 5070 12GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5070 price, TRI FROZR 4 GPU, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, white gaming GPU, RTX 5070 specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Gaming Trio OC White brings NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and DLSS 4 to a bold, all-white aesthetic built for style-matched builds. It features 12GB of GDDR7 memory, 6144 CUDA cores, and factory-overclocked boost speeds up to 2610 MHz, backed by MSI\'s TRI FROZR 4 thermal design with triple STORMFORCE fans for powerful, quiet cooling.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Gaming Trio OC White is built around the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 GPU on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, delivering 6144 CUDA cores alongside 12GB of GDDR7 memory across a 192-bit bus at 28 Gbps. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2610 MHz boost clock in Gaming/Silent mode, climbing to 2625 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — putting it a notch above the standard Inspire and Ventus variants in the RTX 5070 lineup.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution for major gains in frame rate and image quality. NVIDIA Reflex 2 with Frame Warp further reduces input latency for competitive play, while support for the 50-series\' upgraded encode/decode engine benefits creators working in Adobe Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, and similar applications. Display connectivity is upgraded to DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>Part of MSI\'s flagship Gaming Trio line, this card carries an aggressive design accented with diffused LED lighting and a dragon totem motif, finished here in a clean white colorway for style-matched builds. Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 4 thermal design, featuring triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades for high airflow and low noise, a nickel-plated copper baseplate for fast heat capture, square-profile core pipes for maximum GPU contact, Wave Curved 4.0 fin geometry, and Air Antegrade Fin 2.0 V-cut fins to reduce turbulence. A reinforcing metal backplate with vents and thermal pads rounds out the cooling package, while MSI Center and MSI Afterburner provide real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Feature</th><th>Specification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 (GB205-300)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>6144 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2610 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode), up to 2625 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>12GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr>