(1237, 'MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G GAMING TRIO OC GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Gaming Trio OC pairs NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and DLSS 4 with MSI\'s flagship Gaming Trio design — bold lines, dragon-totem RGB lighting, and serious cooling. It features 12GB of GDDR7 memory, 6144 CUDA cores, and factory-overclocked boost speeds up to 2625 MHz, backed by MSI\'s TRI FROZR 4 thermal design with triple STORMFORCE fans.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-5070-12g-gaming-trio-oc-gddr7-graphics-card-1783861105', '<p>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G GAMING X SLIM GDDR6X Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have solid specs on this variant. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G GAMING X SLIM</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 SUPER 12G Gaming X Slim | 12GB GDDR6X Graphics Card</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Buy the MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G Gaming X Slim — 12GB GDDR6X, 7168 CUDA cores, TRI FROZR 3 cooling, DLSS 3, up to 2640 MHz boost clock. Shop now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 SUPER Gaming X Slim, RTX 4070 Super 12GB, MSI RTX 4070 Super price, TRI FROZR 3 graphics card, 12GB GDDR6X GPU, DLSS 3 graphics card, Ada Lovelace GPU, SFF-ready RTX GPU, RTX 4070 Super specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G Gaming X Slim delivers premium 1440p and 4K gaming performance in a compact, SFF-friendly design. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture with 12GB of GDDR6X memory, 7168 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2640 MHz, it\'s cooled by MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design with triple TORX Fan 5.0 blades — combining strong performance, quiet operation, and a slimmer footprint than standard Gaming X cards.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER 12G Gaming X Slim is built around the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER GPU, offering 7168 CUDA cores — 20% more than the standard RTX 4070 — along with 12GB of GDDR6X memory across a 192-bit bus at 21 Gbps. Boost clocks reach 2640 MHz out of the box, with MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode pushing that to 2655 MHz, giving this card the muscle for high-frame-rate 1440p gaming and demanding 4K workloads alike.</p><p>Powered by NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-generation RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing, fourth-generation Tensor Cores paired with an Optical Flow Accelerator for AI-driven DLSS 3 frame generation, and NVIDIA Reflex to minimize system latency for competitive gaming. As part of the \"Gaming Slim\" line, it\'s designed as a thinner variant of the standard Gaming series while still maintaining high performance and an aggressive look, making it a strong fit for small form factor builds. <a href=\"https://www.msi.com/Graphics-Card/GeForce-RTX-4070-SUPER-12G-GAMING-X-SLIM-MLG\">MSI</a></p><p>Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design, featuring TORX Fan 5.0 blades linked by ring arcs and a fan cowl to stabilize and concentrate airflow, a copper baseplate that pulls heat away from the GPU and memory modules, square-shaped core heat pipes for maximum GPU contact, and Airflow Control fin sections that reduce turbulence and noise. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring and tuning, with MSI Afterburner available for more advanced overclocking control, and MSI Mystic Light for customizable RGB lighting synced with other MSI and compatible third-party components.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER (AD104)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>7168 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>56 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>224 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2640 MHz (up to 2655 MHz in Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>12GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>192-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>21 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~504 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v1.4a), 1x HDMI (2.1a — 4K@120Hz HDR, 8K@60Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320 @ 60Hz</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>~245 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>650W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>TRI FROZR 3 with triple TORX Fan 5.0, copper baseplate, core pipes, Airflow Control</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Form Factor</td><td>Gaming Slim (thinner than standard Gaming series), SFF-ready</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Lighting</td><td>MSI Mystic Light RGB</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 3 (AI frame generation)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center, MSI Afterburner</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>Want this expo