h updated ray tracing and Tensor Core hardware for AI-accelerated rendering and content creation. Display output has also been upgraded, with DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b connectors supporting resolutions and refresh rates up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, Gaming VRR, and HDR. <a href=\"https://us-store.msi.com/RTX-5070\">MSI</a></p><p>True to its name, the INSPIRE series pairs a small form factor with strong performance, making it a natural fit for compact builds and creative workstations. Cooling comes from a triple-fan design using seven-blade STORMFORCE fans with claw texturing for optimal airflow and reduced noise, paired with a nickel-plated copper baseplate that captures and transfers heat from the GPU and memory, square-profile core pipes for maximum thermal contact, and WAVE-CURVED 3.0 fin optimization to fine-tune airflow efficiency around the fan motor. A metal backplate with vents and thermal pads rounds out the cooling package. The card is managed through MSI Center, which offers both a Gaming mode for maximum performance and a Silent mode for quieter operation, plus MSI Afterburner for advanced overclocking control. <a href=\"https://us-store.msi.com/RTX-5070\">MSI</a><a href=\"https://videocardz.net/msi-geforce-rtx-5070-12gb-inspire-3x-oc\">VideoCardz</a></p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 (GB205-300)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>6144 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2542 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode), up to 2557 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>12GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>192-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>28 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>~250 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>650W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Length</td><td>288 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Slot Size</td><td>Dual-slot</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x STORMFORCE fans</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>Nickel-plated copper baseplate, square core pipes, WAVE-CURVED 3.0, Air Antegrade Fin</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Backplate</td><td>Metal backplate with vents and thermal pads</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Form Factor</td><td>Compact/SFF-ready design</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center (Gaming/Silent mode), MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>Want this exported as a ready-to-use file (HTML, Markdown, or CSV for a specific platform)?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G GAMING TRIO OC WHITE GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have solid data. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G GAMING TRIO OC WHITE</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</stro