(1238, 'MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G VANGUARD SOC LAUNCH EDITION GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition is MSI\'s premium take on the RTX 5070, built with NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and DLSS 4. It ships with 12GB of GDDR7 memory, 6144 CUDA cores, and a super-overclocked boost speed of 2640 MHz, cooled by MSI\'s flagship Hyper Frozr thermal design with an advanced vapor chamber and triple STORMFORCE fans. The Launch Edition adds unique packaging and a surprise \"Lucky Blind Box\" collectible.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-5070-12g-vanguard-soc-launch-edition-gddr7-graphics-card-1783861171', '<p>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G INSPIRE 3X OC GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have solid data on this one. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G INSPIRE 3X OC</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 12G Inspire 3X OC | 12GB GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Get the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Inspire 3X OC — 12GB GDDR7, Blackwell architecture, DLSS 4, triple STORMFORCE fans, up to 2557 MHz boost. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Inspire 3X OC, RTX 5070 12GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5070 price, Blackwell graphics card, DLSS 4 graphics card, PCIe 5.0 GPU, STORMFORCE fan GPU, SFF-ready graphics card, RTX 5070 specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Inspire 3X OC brings NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and next-gen DLSS 4 to a compact, small-form-factor-friendly design. It features 12GB of GDDR7 memory, 6144 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2557 MHz, cooled by a triple STORMFORCE fan thermal solution — built for creators and gamers who want strong performance without a bulky card.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Inspire 3X OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 GPU, built on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture. It packs 6144 CUDA cores, 12GB of next-gen GDDR7 memory on a 192-bit bus running at 28 Gbps, and a factory-overclocked boost clock of 2542 MHz in Gaming/Silent mode, reaching up to 2557 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode. This marks a generational leap over GDDR6X-based predecessors, delivering higher memory bandwidth for smoother 1440p and 4K gaming.</p><p>Blackwell brings DLSS 4 support to the table, along with updated ray tracing and Tensor Core hardware for AI-accelerated rendering and content creation. Display output has also been upgraded, with DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b connectors supporting resolutions and refresh rates up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, Gaming VRR, and HDR. <a href=\"https://us-store.msi.com/RTX-5070\">MSI</a></p><p>True to its name, the INSPIRE series pairs a small form factor with strong performance, making it a natural fit for compact builds and creative workstations. Cooling comes from a triple-fan design using seven-blade STORMFORCE fans with claw texturing for optimal airflow and reduced noise, paired with a nickel-plated copper baseplate that captures and transfers heat from the GPU and memory, square-profile core pipes for maximum thermal contact, and WAVE-CURVED 3.0 fin optimization to fine-tune airflow efficiency around the fan motor. A metal backplate with vents and thermal pads rounds out the cooling package. The card is managed through MSI Center, which offers both a Gaming mode for maximum performance and a Silent mode for quieter operation, plus MSI Afterburner for advanced overclocking control. <a href=\"https://us-store.msi.com/RTX-5070\">MSI</a><a href=\"https://videocardz.net/msi-geforce-rtx-5070-12gb-inspire-3x-oc\">VideoCardz</a></p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specifica