070 lineup.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution for major gains in frame rate and image quality. NVIDIA Reflex 2 with Frame Warp further reduces input latency for competitive play, while support for the 50-series\' upgraded encode/decode engine benefits creators working in Adobe Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, and similar applications. Display connectivity is upgraded to DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>Part of MSI\'s flagship Gaming Trio line, this card carries an aggressive design accented with diffused LED lighting and a dragon totem motif, finished here in a clean white colorway for style-matched builds. Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 4 thermal design, featuring triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades for high airflow and low noise, a nickel-plated copper baseplate for fast heat capture, square-profile core pipes for maximum GPU contact, Wave Curved 4.0 fin geometry, and Air Antegrade Fin 2.0 V-cut fins to reduce turbulence. A reinforcing metal backplate with vents and thermal pads rounds out the cooling package, while MSI Center and MSI Afterburner provide real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 (GB205-300)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>6144 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2610 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode), up to 2625 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>12GB GDD