5070 lineup, with independent testing showing real-world boost behavior running well above the rated spec under load.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution, along with NVIDIA Reflex 2 and Frame Warp for reduced input latency. Display output is upgraded to DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting resolutions up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>The Vanguard series represents MSI\'s premium design line, with aerodynamic edges, fractured lines, and futuristic RGB lighting running across the card\'s face. Cooling is handled by MSI\'s flagship Hyper Frozr thermal design: triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades for high static pressure, an advanced built-in vapor chamber that rapidly transfers heat from the GPU and VRAM to square-shaped core pipes, filled fins that reduce turbulence, and Wave Curved 4.0 and Air Antegrade Fin 2.0 fin geometry for optimized airflow. This Launch Edition variant adds a distinctive black-and-silver shell with a slicing RGB light bar, unique launch-day packaging, and a surprise \"Lucky Blind Box\" collectible figure included with purchase.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 (GB205-300)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>6144 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>48 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>192 (5th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2640 MHz (SOC), up to 2655 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td>