264 Tensor cores, paired with 16GB of GDDR6X memory on a 256-bit bus running at 21 Gbps for roughly 672 GB/s of memory bandwidth. Boost clocks reach 2625 MHz (2610 MHz standard boost), giving it strong performance for high-refresh 1440p and demanding 4K gaming.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, alongside NVIDIA Reflex for reduced system latency. As part of the Gaming Slim family, it keeps a thinner profile than MSI\'s standard Gaming line while maintaining strong cooling and performance headroom.</p><p>Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design, with TORX Fan 5.0 blades linked by ring arcs and a fan cowl for stabilized, high-pressure airflow, a nickel-plated copper baseplate to quickly pull heat from the GPU and memory, square-shaped core heat pipes for maximum GPU contact, and Airflow Control fin sections to direct air where it\'s needed most. The card also includes MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature, which stops the fans entirely at low temperatures for silent idle operation. Many retail bundles pair this card with a download code for S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2: Heart of Chornobyl Deluxe Edition, letting buyers jump straight into the game the card was designed around.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (AD103-275)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process (TSMC 4N)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8448 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>66 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>264 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2610 M