(1240, 'MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G VENTUS 3X PZ OC 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC pairs NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture with MSI\'s Project Zero design, hiding the power connector behind the board for a clean, cable-free look from the front. It offers 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 8960 CUDA cores, and a factory overclock up to 2497 MHz, backed by a robust triple-fan cooling solution — all built to NVIDIA SFF specifications.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-5070-ti-16g-ventus-3x-pz-oc-16gb-gddr7-graphics-card-1783861337', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti GPU, built on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture with 8960 CUDA cores. It\'s equipped with 16GB of GDDR7 memory across a 256-bit bus at 28 Gbps, delivering roughly 896 GB/s of memory bandwidth. The card ships with a factory overclock, hitting a 2482 MHz boost clock (about 1% above reference) and reaching up to 2497 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode.</p><p>What sets this card apart from the standard Ventus 3X OC is MSI\'s Project Zero design. Rather than routing power cables over the top of the card, the 12VHPWR connection is moved to a rear-facing dongle behind a removable magnetic backplate, keeping the front of the card free of visible cabling for a cleaner build. The card still conforms to NVIDIA\'s SFF (small form factor) specifications, making it a strong fit for compact cases that prioritize both airflow and aesthetics.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution, along with NVIDIA Reflex 2 for reduced latency. Display output includes DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>As part of MSI\'s Ventus line, the card keeps a neutral, understated aesthetic without RGB lighting, letting it blend into any build. Cooling comes from triple TORX Fan 5.0 blades, a copper heatsink baseplate, and square-profile core heat pipes that directly contact the baseplate for efficient heat transfer, plus a vented backplate to aid airflow. MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature shuts the fans off entirely at low temperatures for silent idle operation, and the card is backed by MSI Center for monitoring and tuning plus MSI Afterburner for advanced overclocking control.</p>', '<p>Great data, including a detailed review. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G VENTUS 3X PZ OC</strong>:</p><h3>Meta Title</h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC | 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><h3>Meta Description</h3><p>Buy the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC — 16GB GDDR7, Project Zero clean-cable design, DLSS 4, up to 2497 MHz boost clock. Shop now!</p><h3>Meta Keywords</h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Ti Ventus 3X PZ OC, Project Zero graphics card, RTX 5070 Ti 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5070 Ti price, clean cable GPU design, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, SFF-ready RTX GPU, RTX 5070 Ti specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3>Short Description</h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC pairs NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture with MSI\'s Project Zero design, hiding the power connector behind the board for a clean, cable-free look from the front. It offers 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 8960 CUDA cores, and a factory overclock up to 2497 MHz, backed by a robust triple-fan cooling solution — all built to NVIDIA SFF specifications.</p><h3>Long Description</h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti GPU, built on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture with 8960 CUDA cores. It\'s equipped with 16GB of GDDR7 memory across a 256-bit bus at 28 Gbps, delivering roughly 896 GB/s of memory bandwidth. The card ships with a factory overclock, hitting a 2482 MHz boost clock (about 1% above reference) and reaching up to 2497 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode.</p><p>What sets this card apart from the standard Ventus 3X OC is MSI\'s Project Zero design. Rather than routing power cables over the top of the card, the 12VHPWR connection is moved to a rear-facing dongle behind a removable magnetic backplate, keeping the front of the card free of visible cabling for a cleaner build. The card still conforms to NVIDIA\'s SFF (small form factor) specifications, making it a strong fit for compact cases that prioritize both airflow and aesthetics.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution, along with NVIDIA Reflex 2 for reduced latency. Display output includes DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>As part of MSI\'s Ventus line, the card keeps a neutral, understated aesthetic without RGB lighting, letting it blend into any build. Cooling comes from triple TORX Fan 5.0 blades, a copper heatsink baseplate, and square-profile core heat pipes that directly contact the baseplate for efficient heat transfer, plus a vented backplate to aid airflow. MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature shuts the fans off entirely at low temperatures for silent idle operation, and the card is backed by MSI Center for monitoring and tuning plus MSI Afterburner for advanced overclocking control.</p><h3>Specifications</h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Feature</th><th>Specification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8960 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2482 MHz (~1% OC), up to 2497 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>28 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~896 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR, rear-facing Project Zero dongle)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>300 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>750W and above (ATX 3.1 recommended)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>303 x 121 x 49 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Weight (Card/Package)</td><td>1077 g / 1555 g</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x TORX Fan 5.0</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>Copper baseplate, square core heat pipes, vented backplate, ZERO FROZR</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Special Design</td><td>Project Zero — rear power connector, removable magnetic backplate, clean-cable aesthetic</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Form Factor</td><td>NVIDIA SFF-compliant</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center, MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', 'Graphics Card', 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/JNZVrgjz9PgzfN3KYrbao8iIU87KawIEsYb1dMAx.webp', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 13:02:17', '2026-07-12 13:02:17', 'MSI RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC | 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'vBuy the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC — 16GB GDDR7, Project Zero clean-cable design, DLSS 4, up to 2497 MHz boost clock. Shop now!', 'MSI RTX 5070 Ti Ventus 3X PZ OC, Project Zero graphics card, RTX 5070 Ti 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5070 Ti price, clean cable GPU design, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, SFF-ready RTX GPU, RTX 5070 Ti specs, MSI graphics card 2026', NULL, 14, NULL, NULL);
