(1241, 'MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G SHADOW 3X OC GDDR6X Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Shadow 3X OC brings a darker, stealthier color scheme to MSI\'s Ventus-based design, trading silver accents for a bronze metallic finish. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, it delivers 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 8448 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2655 MHz — all in a notably thin and light card that\'s well suited to compact builds.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-4070-ti-super-16g-shadow-3x-oc-gddr6x-graphics-card-1783861388', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Shadow 3X OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER GPU (AD103), featuring 8448 CUDA cores, 66 ray tracing cores, and 264 Tensor cores. It\'s paired with 16GB of GDDR6X memory on a 256-bit bus at 21 Gbps, delivering roughly 672 GB/s of memory bandwidth. The card ships with a factory-overclocked boost speed of 2640 MHz, reaching up to 2655 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — a 1.7% bump over the reference 2610 MHz clock.</p><p>Visually, the Shadow 3X is essentially a restyled Ventus 3X, swapping the silver tones of that line for a darker bronze and brown metallic finish for a stealthier look. It\'s also notably thinner and lighter than the standard Ventus 3X — 43mm thick and roughly 838 grams versus 50mm and 1107 grams — while keeping the same core cooling hardware, making it a strong choice for slim or ITX-style builds.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, along with NVIDIA Reflex for reduced system latency. Cooling comes from a triple TORX Fan 4.0 setup, a copper baseplate, and heat pipes that run the full length of the GPU for efficient heat transfer, plus MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature, which shuts the fans off entirely once temperatures drop below a set threshold for silent idle operation. The card also includes a reinforced backplate and a bundled support bracket to guard against GPU sag, and is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking.</p>', '<p>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G VANGUARD SOC LAUNCH EDITION GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have thorough data on this one, including from the LDLC/Overclockers review. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G VANGUARD SOC LAUNCH EDITION</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 12G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition | 12GB GDDR7 GPU</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Get the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition — 12GB GDDR7, Hyper Frozr cooling, DLSS 4, up to 2640 MHz boost, includes Lucky Blind Box. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Vanguard SOC, Vanguard Launch Edition GPU, RTX 5070 12GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5070 price, Hyper Frozr thermal design, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, vapor chamber GPU cooling, RTX 5070 specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition is MSI\'s premium take on the RTX 5070, built with NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and DLSS 4. It ships with 12GB of GDDR7 memory, 6144 CUDA cores, and a super-overclocked boost speed of 2640 MHz, cooled by MSI\'s flagship Hyper Frozr thermal design with an advanced vapor chamber and triple STORMFORCE fans. The Launch Edition adds unique packaging and a surprise \"Lucky Blind Box\" collectible.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 12G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 GPU on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, featuring 6144 CUDA cores, 48 ray tracing cores, and 192 Tensor cores. It\'s paired with 12GB of GDDR7 memory on a 192-bit bus at 28 Gbps, delivering roughly 672 GB/s of memory bandwidth. As MSI\'s Super Overclocked (SOC) flagship variant, it ships with a 2640 MHz boost clock, reaching up to 2655 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — among the highest factory clocks in the RTX 5070 lineup, with independent testing showing real-world boost behavior running well above the rated spec under load.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution, along with NVIDIA Reflex 2 and Frame Warp for reduced input latency. Display output is upgraded to DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting resolutions up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>The Vanguard series represents MSI\'s premium design line, with aerodynamic edges, fractured lines, and futuristic RGB lighting running across the card\'s face. Cooling is handled by MSI\'s flagship Hyper Frozr thermal design: triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades for high static pressure, an advanced built-in vapor chamber that rapidly transfers heat from the GPU and VRAM to square-shaped core pipes, filled fins that reduce turbulence, and Wave Curved 4.0 and Air Antegrade Fin 2.0 fin geometry for optimized airflow. This Launch Edition variant adds a distinctive black-and-silver shell with a slicing RGB light bar, unique launch-day packaging, and a surprise \"Lucky Blind Box\" collectible figure included with purchase.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 (GB205-300)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>6144 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>48 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>192 (5th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2640 MHz (SOC), up to 2655 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>12GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>192-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>28 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~672 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR, ATX 3.1 PSU recommended)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>250 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>650W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>337 x 140 x 61 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Weight (Card/Package)</td><td>1503 g / 2296 g</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Color</td><td>Black with RGB accent</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x STORMFORCE fans</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>Hyper Frozr Thermal Design — vapor chamber, square core pipes, filled fins, Wave Curved 4.0, Air Antegrade Fin 2.0</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Special Edition</td><td>Launch Edition packaging + Lucky Blind Box collectible</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2 (Frame Warp)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center, MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>Want this exported as a ready-to-use file (HTML, Markdown, or CSV for a specific platform)?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G GAMING X SLIM STALKER 2 EDITION 16GB GDDR6X Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Excellent data on this one. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G GAMING X SLIM STALKER 2 EDITION</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming Slim STALKER 2 Edition GPU</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Shop the MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming Slim STALKER 2 Edition — 16GB GDDR6X, 8448 CUDA cores, DLSS 3, unique S.T.A.L.K.E.R. universe design. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super STALKER 2, STALKER 2 graphics card, RTX 4070 Ti Super 16GB, MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super price, S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2 GPU edition, TRI FROZR 3 graphics card, DLSS 3 graphics card, Ada Lovelace GPU, RTX 4070 Ti Super specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming Slim STALKER 2 Edition is a co-branded graphics card created with S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2: Heart of Chornobyl, featuring the game\'s distinctive color scheme. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, it offers 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 8448 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2625 MHz, cooled by MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design — a standout pick for gamers who want performance and personality in one package.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>Created through a partnership between MSI and GSC Game World, this special edition graphics card carries the unique green-and-orange color scheme of the S.T.A.L.K.E.R. universe, giving fans of the franchise a way to bring that aesthetic straight into their build. It\'s based on the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER, featuring the AD103 GPU with 8448 CUDA cores, 66 ray tracing cores, and 264 Tensor cores, paired with 16GB of GDDR6X memory on a 256-bit bus running at 21 Gbps for roughly 672 GB/s of memory bandwidth. Boost clocks reach 2625 MHz (2610 MHz standard boost), giving it strong performance for high-refresh 1440p and demanding 4K gaming.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, alongside NVIDIA Reflex for reduced system latency. As part of the Gaming Slim family, it keeps a thinner profile than MSI\'s standard Gaming line while maintaining strong cooling and performance headroom.</p><p>Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design, with TORX Fan 5.0 blades linked by ring arcs and a fan cowl for stabilized, high-pressure airflow, a nickel-plated copper baseplate to quickly pull heat from the GPU and memory, square-shaped core heat pipes for maximum GPU contact, and Airflow Control fin sections to direct air where it\'s needed most. The card also includes MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature, which stops the fans entirely at low temperatures for silent idle operation. Many retail bundles pair this card with a download code for S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2: Heart of Chornobyl Deluxe Edition, letting buyers jump straight into the game the card was designed around.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (AD103-275)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process (TSMC 4N)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8448 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>66 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>264 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2610 MHz (up to 2625 MHz Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>21 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~672 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v1.4a), 1x HDMI (2.1a — 4K@120Hz HDR, 8K@60Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>285 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>700W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>307 mm length, 2.6-slot</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Weight</td><td>~1094 g</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Color Scheme</td><td>Green / Orange (S.T.A.L.K.E.R. themed)</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x TORX Fan 5.0</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>TRI FROZR 3, nickel-plated copper baseplate, square core heat pipes, Airflow Control, ZERO FROZR</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Special Edition</td><td>Co-branded S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2 design; select bundles include game download code</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Softwar