ation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center, MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>Want this exported as a ready-to-use file (HTML, Markdown, or CSV for a specific platform)?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G SHADOW 3X OC GDDR6X Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Great data. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G SHADOW 3X OC</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Shadow 3X OC | 16GB GDDR6X GPU</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Get the MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Shadow 3X OC — 16GB GDDR6X, stealthy bronze design, DLSS 3, up to 2655 MHz boost clock, slim build. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super Shadow 3X OC, Shadow 3X graphics card, RTX 4070 Ti Super 16GB, MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super price, stealth GPU design, DLSS 3 graphics card, Ada Lovelace GPU, slim graphics card, RTX 4070 Ti Super specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Shadow 3X OC brings a darker, stealthier color scheme to MSI\'s Ventus-based design, trading silver accents for a bronze metallic finish. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, it delivers 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 8448 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2655 MHz — all in a notably thin and light card that\'s well suited to compact builds.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Shadow 3X OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER GPU (AD103), featuring 8448 CUDA cores, 66 ray tracing cores, and 264 Tensor cores. It\'s paired with 16GB of GDDR6X memory on a 256-bit bus at 21 Gbps, delivering roughly 672 GB/s of memory bandwidth. The card ships with a factory-overclocked boost speed of 2640 MHz, reaching up to 2655 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — a 1.7% bump over the reference 2610 MHz clock.</p><p>Visually, the Shadow 3X is essentially a restyled Ventus 3X, swapping the silver tones of that line for a darker bronze and brown metallic finish for a stealthier look. It\'s also notably thinner and lighter than the standard Ventus 3X — 43mm thick and roughly 838 grams versus 50mm and 1107 grams — while keeping the same core cooling hardware, making it a strong choice for slim or ITX-style builds.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, along with NVIDIA Reflex for reduced system latency. Cooling comes from a triple TORX Fan 4.0 setup, a copper baseplate, and heat pipes that run the full length of the GPU for efficient heat transfer, plus MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature, which shuts the fans off entirely once temperatures drop below a set threshold for silent idle operation. The card also includes a reinforced backplate and a bundled support bracket to guard against GPU sag, and is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (AD103-275)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8448 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>66 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>264 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</t