(1243, 'MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G VENTUS 2X OC GDDR6X Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Ventus 2X OC delivers the full performance of the RTX 4070 Ti SUPER in a compact dual-fan design, ideal for builds with tighter case clearance. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, it offers 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 8448 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2655 MHz, backed by MSI\'s TORX Fan 4.0 cooling and a sharp, understated aesthetic.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-4070-ti-super-16g-ventus-2x-oc-gddr6x-graphics-card-1783861540', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Ventus 2X OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER GPU (AD103), delivering 8448 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR6X memory on a 256-bit bus at 21 Gbps. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2640 MHz boost clock, reaching up to 2655 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode, giving it the same clock speeds as MSI\'s triple-fan Ventus 3X variant in a noticeably shorter card.</p><p>At just 242mm long, this dual-fan design trades a slightly larger footprint for compact dimensions that fit more easily into mid-tower and smaller cases without giving up factory-overclocked performance. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, along with NVIDIA Reflex for reduced system latency.</p><p>As part of MSI\'s Ventus line, the card carries a sharp, understated design that fits into any build without demanding attention. Cooling comes from dual TORX Fan 4.0 blades that work in pairs for focused, high-pressure airflow, Airflow Control deflectors that direct air where it\'s needed most, and precision-crafted heat pipes that maximize contact with the GPU and spread heat across the full heatsink. MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature stops the fans completely at low temperatures for silent idle operation, and the card is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p>', '<p>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G VENTUS 3X PZ OC 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Great data, including a detailed review. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G VENTUS 3X PZ OC</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC | 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Buy the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC — 16GB GDDR7, Project Zero clean-cable design, DLSS 4, up to 2497 MHz boost clock. Shop now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Ti Ventus 3X PZ OC, Project Zero graphics card, RTX 5070 Ti 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5070 Ti price, clean cable GPU design, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, SFF-ready RTX GPU, RTX 5070 Ti specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC pairs NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture with MSI\'s Project Zero design, hiding the power connector behind the board for a clean, cable-free look from the front. It offers 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 8960 CUDA cores, and a factory overclock up to 2497 MHz, backed by a robust triple-fan cooling solution — all built to NVIDIA SFF specifications.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Ventus 3X PZ OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti GPU, built on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture with 8960 CUDA cores. It\'s equipped with 16GB of GDDR7 memory across a 256-bit bus at 28 Gbps, delivering roughly 896 GB/s of memory bandwidth. The card ships with a factory overclock, hitting a 2482 MHz boost clock (about 1% above reference) and reaching up to 2497 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode.</p><p>What sets this card apart from the standard Ventus 3X OC is MSI\'s Project Zero design. Rather than routing power cables over the top of the card, the 12VHPWR connection is moved to a rear-facing dongle behind a removable magnetic backplate, keeping the front of the card free of visible cabling for a cleaner build. The card still conforms to NVIDIA\'s SFF (small form factor) specifications, making it a strong fit for compact cases that prioritize both airflow and aesthetics.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution, along with NVIDIA Reflex 2 for reduced latency. Display output includes DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>As part of MSI\'s Ventus line, the card keeps a neutral, understated aesthetic without RGB lighting, letting it blend into any build. Cooling comes from triple TORX Fan 5.0 blades, a copper heatsink baseplate, and square-profile core heat pipes that directly contact the baseplate for efficient heat transfer, plus a vented backplate to aid airflow. MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature shuts the fans off entirely at low temperatures for silent idle operation, and the card is backed by MSI Center for monitoring and tuning plus MSI Afterburner for advanced overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8960 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2482 MHz (~1% OC), up to 2497 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR7</td></tr><t