(1246, 'MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G GAMING X SLIM GDDR6X Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming X Slim delivers premium 1440p and 4K gaming performance in a thinner, more aggressive-looking chassis than MSI\'s standard Gaming line. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture with 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 8448 CUDA cores, and one of the highest factory boost clocks in the RTX 4070 Ti SUPER lineup at up to 2685 MHz, it\'s cooled by MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design for quiet, efficient performance.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-4070-ti-super-16g-gaming-x-slim-gddr6x-graphics-card-1783862145', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming X Slim is built around the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER GPU, delivering 8448 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR6X memory across a 256-bit bus at 21 Gbps. The card ships with an aggressive factory overclock, hitting a 2670 MHz boost clock and reaching up to 2685 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — among the highest clocks offered across MSI\'s RTX 4070 Ti SUPER variants, ahead of both the standard Gaming Slim and Ventus 3X models.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, along with NVIDIA Reflex for reduced system latency. Owners consistently note it handles demanding titles comfortably at 1440p and 4K with headroom to spare, thanks to the ample 16GB VRAM buffer.</p><p>As part of the \"Gaming Slim\" line, this card is a noticeably thinner variant of MSI\'s standard Gaming series while retaining high performance and an aggressive aesthetic, with tasteful RGB accenting the manufacturer logo rather than dominating the design. Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design, which channels heat from the GPU to all heat pipes efficiently for consistently cool, quiet operation, complemented by MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature that stops the fans completely at low temperatures for silent idle use. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring and tuning, with MSI Afterburner available for more advanced overclocking control.</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Feature</th><th>Specification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (AD103-275)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8448 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>66 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>264 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2670 MHz (up to 2685 MHz Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>21 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~672 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v1.4a), 1x HDMI (2.1a — 4K@120Hz HDR, 8K@60Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>285 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>700W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Form Factor</td><td>Slim design (thinner than standard Gaming series)</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Lighting</td><td>Minimal RGB (manufacturer logo accent)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>TRI FROZR 3, ZERO FROZR</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Design Language</td><td>Aggressive Gaming Slim aesthetic</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 3 (AI frame generation)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center, MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', NULL, 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/aa5gfO4IifGL8P6QyegwKo5by3ogCcE69MYhB4zB.webp', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 13:15:45', '2026-07-12 13:15:45', 'MSI RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming X Slim | 16GB GDDR6X GPU', 'Shop the MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming X Slim — 16GB GDDR6X, TRI FROZR 3 cooling, DLSS 3, up to 2670 MHz boost clock, slim aggressive design. Buy now!', 'MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super Gaming X Slim, RTX 4070 Ti Super 16GB, MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super price, TRI FROZR 3 graphics card, DLSS 3 graphics card, Ada Lovelace GPU, slim gaming GPU, RTX 4070 Ti Super specs, MSI graphics card 2026, 16GB VRAM graphics card', NULL, 14, NULL, NULL),
(1247, 'MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G EXPERT GDDR6X Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Expert brings a distinctive push-pull airflow cooling system and premium aluminum alloy casing to MSI\'s high-end lineup. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, it offers 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 8448 CUDA cores, and one of the highest factory boost clocks in the RTX 4070 Ti SUPER family at up to 2685 MHz — combining refined looks with serious performance for gamers and creators.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-4070-ti-super-16g-expert-gddr6x-graphics-card-1783862237', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Expert is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER GPU, delivering 8448 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR6X memory across a 256-bit bus at 21 Gbps. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2670 MHz boost clock, reaching up to 2685 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode, matching the top clocks found on MSI\'s Gaming X Slim variant.</p><p>Part of MSI\'s Expert series, this card is built around a distinctive push-pull airflow system, where two sets of fans work together — one pushing cool air into the heatsink while the other pulls hot air away — for improved cooling efficiency and reduced heat buildup. A patented fan design gives the card a distinctive appearance while further enhancing heat dissipation. The card\'s aluminum alloy casing adds durability and stability while giving it a refined, premium look that sets it apart from MSI\'s standard gaming-branded cards.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, along with NVIDIA Reflex for reduced input latency. Cooling is further supported by a copper baseplate that captures heat from the GPU and memory modules and rapidly transfers it to core pipes, along with dual ball-bearing fans and MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature for silent idle operation. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring and tuning, with MSI Afterburner and its OC Scanner feature available for automated, stable overclocking.</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Feature</th><th>Specification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (AD103-275)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8448 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>66 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>264 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2670 MHz (up to 2685 MHz Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>21 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~672 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v1.4a), 1x HDMI (2.1a — 4K@120Hz HDR, 8K@60Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>285 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>700W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Build Material</td><td>Aluminum alloy casing</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fan Bearings</td><td>Dual ball-bearing fans</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>FLOW FROZR push-pull airflow, patented fan design, copper baseplate, ZERO FROZR</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Design Language</td><td>Premium/refined Expert series aesthetic</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 3 (AI frame generation)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center, MSI Afterburner (with OC Scanner)</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', 'Graphics Card', 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/xofOUKH3cxYN7qZ9Og2he5mVJ76nwJrCZx4UHkJN.webp', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 13:17:17', '2026-07-12 13:17:17', 'MSI RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Expert | 16GB GDDR6X Graphics Card', 'Get the MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Expert — 16GB GDDR6X, push-pull airflow cooling, DLSS 3, up to 2685 MHz boost, premium aluminum design. Buy now!', 'MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super Expert, Expert series graphics card, RTX 4070 Ti Super 16GB, MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super price, push-pull airflow GPU, DLSS 3 graphics card, Ada Lovelace GPU, premium aluminum GPU, RTX 4070 Ti Super specs, MSI graphics card 2026', NULL, 14, NULL, NULL),
(1248, 'MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G GAMING TRIO OC PLUS 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Gaming Trio OC Plus is the factory-overclocked, premium variant of MSI\'s Gaming Trio Plus lineup, pairing NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and DLSS 4 with a reinforced PCB and top-tier cooling. It features 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 8960 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2580 MHz, backed by MSI\'s TRI FROZR 4 thermal design with triple STORMFORCE fans and extra electrical protection for sustained, reliable performance.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-5070-ti-16g-gaming-trio-oc-plus-16gb-gddr7-graphics-card-1783862328', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Gaming Trio OC Plus is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti GPU (GB203) on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, delivering 8960 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR7 memory across a 256-bit bus at 28 Gbps. As the factory-overclocked \"Plus\" variant, it ships with a 2572 MHz boost clock in Gaming/Silent mode, reaching up to 2580 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — a meaningful step up from the standard Gaming Trio Plus card\'s 2452 MHz boost clock.</p><p>What sets the \"Plus\" apart from the standard Gaming Trio OC is a reinforced custom PCB, featuring a 2 oz copper layer for improved heat dissipation and reliability, along with additional fuses for electrical protection under sustained heavy loads. This makes it a strong pick for extended gaming sessions, streaming, or demanding creative workloads where consistent power delivery matters.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution for major gains in frame rate and image quality, alongside NVIDIA Reflex 2 for reduced input latency. Display connectivity includes DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>As part of MSI\'s flagship Gaming Trio line, the card carries a fierce, sharp-edged design with diffused LED lighting and a dragon totem motif. Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 4 thermal design, featuring triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades and double ball bearings for durability, a nickel-plated copper baseplate for fast heat capture, square-profile core pipes running the full length of the board, and an Airflow Control radiator with Antegrade 2.0 fins to reduce turbulence. A perforated metal backplate reinforces the chassis while helping release trapped heat, and a bundled support bracket helps prevent GPU sag. The card is managed through MSI Center\'s Gaming and Silent modes plus MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Feature</th><th>Specification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (GB203)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8960 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>280</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2572 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode), up to 2580 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>28 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>~300 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>750W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>338 mm length, 2.5-slot</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Weight</td><td>~1310 g</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x STORMFORCE fans (double ball bearing)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>TRI FROZR 4, nickel-plated copper baseplate, full-length core pipes, Airflow Control radiator (Antegrade 2.0 fins)</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>PCB</td><td>Reinforced with 2 oz copper layer and additional protective fuses</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Backplate</td><td>Perforated metal backplate</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Included Accessories</td><td>Support bracket (anti-sag)</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Lighting</td><td>Diffused LED lighting with dragon totem accent</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center (Gaming/Silent mode), MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', 'Graphics Card', 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/OcE7DRG4iTSSDFVMQcJl3Eu2KfEKTr9HHCiSO52d.webp', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 13:18:48', '2026-07-12 13:18:48', 'MSI RTX 5070 Ti 16G Gaming Trio OC Plus | 16GB GDDR7 GPU', 'Buy the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Gaming Trio OC Plus — 16GB GDDR7, TRI FROZR 4 cooling, DLSS 4, up to 2580 MHz boost clock, premium PCB design. Shop now!', 'MSI RTX 5070 Ti Gaming Trio OC Plus, RTX 5070 Ti 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5070 Ti price, TRI FROZR 4 graphics card, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, STORMFORCE fan GPU, RTX 5070 Ti specs, MSI graphics card 2026, PCIe 5.0 graphics card', NULL, 14, NULL, NULL),
(1249, 'MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G VANGUARD SOC LAUNCH EDITION 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition is MSI\'s flagship RTX 5070 Ti offering, built on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture with DLSS 4. It ships with 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 8960 CUDA cores, and a heavily factory-overclocked boost speed of 2588 MHz, cooled by MSI\'s hefty Hyper Frozr thermal design with triple STORMFORCE fans. The Launch Edition adds unique packaging and a surprise \"Lucky Blind Box\" collectible figure.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-5070-ti-16g-vanguard-soc-launch-edition-16gb-gddr7-graphics-card-1783862468', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti GPU (GB203) on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, featuring 8960 CUDA cores, 70 ray tracing cores, and 280 Tensor cores. It\'s paired with 16GB of GDDR7 memory on a 256-bit bus at 28 Gbps, delivering roughly 896 GB/s of memory bandwidth. As MSI\'s Super Overclocked (SOC) flagship variant, it ships with a 2588 MHz boost clock — a 5.5% jump over NVIDIA\'s 2452 MHz reference spec — reaching up to 2602 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode.</p><p>Within MSI\'s RTX 5070 Ti lineup, which spans Ventus, Gaming Trio, Vanguard, Inspire, and Shadow series, the Vanguard line sits just below MSI\'s premium Suprim series, sharing a similarly refined build quality but with a darker aesthetic, more RGB accenting, and its own factory clock tuning. The SOC designation marks this as the highest factory-overclocked model in the Vanguard range, while the Launch Edition designation specifically adds a limited-run bundle: a \"Lucky\" figurine blind box containing one of ten collectible designs (including a rare secret edition) tied to MSI\'s \"Lucky Around the World\" launch campaign — the underlying card and cooling hardware are otherwise identical to the standard Vanguard SOC.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution, along with NVIDIA Reflex 2 for reduced input latency. Display output is upgraded to DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting resolutions up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>The Vanguard series carries MSI\'s premium design language, with aerodynamic edges, carbon fiber-inspired shroud patterns, and generous RGB lighting throughout. Cooling comes from MSI\'s substantial Hyper Frozr thermal design — a sizeable 357 x 151 x 66mm cooler featuring triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades, a large integrated vapor chamber paired with square-shaped core pipes for enhanced heat dissipation, and a metal backplate for structural reinforcement. A physical Gaming/Silent mode switch along the card\'s edge lets users toggle between BIOS profiles, with Silent mode using a gentler fan curve for quieter operation. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring, RGB customization, and tuning, plus MSI Afterburner for advanced overclocking control.</p>', '<p>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G GAMING X SLIM GDDR6X Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have solid data on this one. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G GAMING X SLIM</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming X Slim | 16GB GDDR6X GPU</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Shop the MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming X Slim — 16GB GDDR6X, TRI FROZR 3 cooling, DLSS 3, up to 2670 MHz boost clock, slim aggressive design. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super Gaming X Slim, RTX 4070 Ti Super 16GB, MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super price, TRI FROZR 3 graphics card, DLSS 3 graphics card, Ada Lovelace GPU, slim gaming GPU, RTX 4070 Ti Super specs, MSI graphics card 2026, 16GB VRAM graphics card</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming X Slim delivers premium 1440p and 4K gaming performance in a thinner, more aggressive-looking chassis than MSI\'s standard Gaming line. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture with 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 8448 CUDA cores, and one of the highest factory boost clocks in the RTX 4070 Ti SUPER lineup at up to 2685 MHz, it\'s cooled by MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design for quiet, efficient performance.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Gaming X Slim is built around the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER GPU, delivering 8448 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR6X memory across a 256-bit bus at 21 Gbps. The card ships with an aggressive factory overclock, hitting a 2670 MHz boost clock and reaching up to 2685 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — among the highest clocks offered across MSI\'s RTX 4070 Ti SUPER variants, ahead of both the standard Gaming Slim and Ventus 3X models.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, along with NVIDIA Reflex for reduced system latency. Owners consistently note it handles demanding titles comfortably at 1440p and 4K with headroom to spare, thanks to the ample 16GB VRAM buffer.</p><p>As part of the \"Gaming Slim\" line, this card is a noticeably thinner variant of MSI\'s standard Gaming series while retaining high performance and an aggressive aesthetic, with tasteful RGB accenting the manufacturer logo rather than dominating the design. Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 3 thermal design, which channels heat from the GPU to all heat pipes efficiently for consistently cool, quiet operation, complemented by MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature that stops the fans completely at low temperatures for silent idle use. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring and tuning, with MSI Afterburner available for more advanced overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (AD103-275)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8448 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>66 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>264 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2670 MHz (up to 2685 MHz Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>21 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~672 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v1.4a), 1x HDMI (2.1a — 4K@120Hz HDR, 8K@60Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>285 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>700W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Form Factor</td><td>Slim design (thinner than standard Gaming series)</td></tr><tr><td>Physical