, it offers 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 8448 CUDA cores, and one of the highest factory boost clocks in the RTX 4070 Ti SUPER family at up to 2685 MHz — combining refined looks with serious performance for gamers and creators.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Expert is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER GPU, delivering 8448 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR6X memory across a 256-bit bus at 21 Gbps. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2670 MHz boost clock, reaching up to 2685 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode, matching the top clocks found on MSI\'s Gaming X Slim variant.</p><p>Part of MSI\'s Expert series, this card is built around a distinctive push-pull airflow system, where two sets of fans work together — one pushing cool air into the heatsink while the other pulls hot air away — for improved cooling efficiency and reduced heat buildup. A patented fan design gives the card a distinctive appearance while further enhancing heat dissipation. The card\'s aluminum alloy casing adds durability and stability while giving it a refined, premium look that sets it apart from MSI\'s standard gaming-branded cards.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, along with NVIDIA Reflex for reduced input latency. Cooling is further supported by a copper baseplate that captures heat from the GPU and memory modules and rapidly transfers it to core pipes, along with dual ball-bearing fans and MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature for silent idle operation. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring and tuning, with MSI Afterburner and its OC Scanner feature available for automated, stable overclocking.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (AD103-275)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8448 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>66 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>264 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2670 MHz (up to 2685 MHz Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>21 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~672 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v1.4a), 1x HDMI (2.1a — 4K@120Hz HDR, 8K@60Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>285 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>700W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Build Material</td><td>Aluminum alloy casing</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fan Bearings</td><td>Dual ball-bearing fans</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>FLOW FROZR push-pull airflow, patented fan design, copper baseplate, ZERO FROZR</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Design Language</td><td>Premium/refined Expert series aesthetic</td></tr