strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Gaming Trio OC Plus is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti GPU (GB203) on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, delivering 8960 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR7 memory across a 256-bit bus at 28 Gbps. As the factory-overclocked \"Plus\" variant, it ships with a 2572 MHz boost clock in Gaming/Silent mode, reaching up to 2580 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — a meaningful step up from the standard Gaming Trio Plus card\'s 2452 MHz boost clock.</p><p>What sets the \"Plus\" apart from the standard Gaming Trio OC is a reinforced custom PCB, featuring a 2 oz copper layer for improved heat dissipation and reliability, along with additional fuses for electrical protection under sustained heavy loads. This makes it a strong pick for extended gaming sessions, streaming, or demanding creative workloads where consistent power delivery matters.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution for major gains in frame rate and image quality, alongside NVIDIA Reflex 2 for reduced input latency. Display connectivity includes DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>As part of MSI\'s flagship Gaming Trio line, the card carries a fierce, sharp-edged design with diffused LED lighting and a dragon totem motif. Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 4 thermal design, featuring triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades and double ball bearings for durability, a nickel-plated copper baseplate for fast heat capture, square-profile core pipes running the full length of the board, and an Airflow Control radiator with Antegrade 2.0 fins to reduce turbulence. A perforated metal backplate reinforces the chassis while helping release trapped heat, and a bundled support bracket helps prevent GPU sag. The card is managed through MSI Center\'s Gaming and Silent modes plus MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (GB203)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8960 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>280</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2572 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode), up to 2580 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>28 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>~300 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>750W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>338 mm length, 2.5-slot</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Weight</td><td>~1310 g</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x STORMFORCE fans (double ball bearing)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>TRI FROZR 4, nickel-plated copper baseplate, full-length core pipes, Airflow Control radiator (Antegrade 2.0 fins)</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>PCB</td><td>Reinforced with 2 oz copper layer and additional protective fuses</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Backplate</td><td>Perforated metal backplate</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Included Accessories</td><td>Support bracket (anti-sag)</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Lighting</td><td>Diffused LED lighting with dragon totem accent</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center (Gaming/Silent mode), MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>Want this exported as a ready-to-use file (HTML, Markdown, or CSV for a specific platform)? I can also compile everything we\'ve covered so far into one catalog file if that would help your workflow.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G VANGUARD SOC LAUNCH EDITION 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Excellent, thorough data across multiple detailed reviews. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G VANGUARD SOC LAUNCH EDITION</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Ti 16G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition | 16GB GDDR7 GPU</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Get the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition — 16GB GDDR7, Hyper Frozr cooling, DLSS 4, up to 2602 MHz boost, includes Lucky Blind Box. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5070 Ti Vanguard SOC, Vanguard Launch Edition GPU, RTX 5070 Ti 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5070 Ti price, Hyper Frozr thermal design, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, premium graphics card, RTX 5070 Ti specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition is MSI\'s flagship RTX 5070 Ti offering, built on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture with DLSS 4. It ships with 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 8960 CUDA cores, and a heavily factory-overclocked boost speed of 2588 MHz, cooled by MSI\'s hefty Hyper Frozr thermal design with triple STORMFORCE fans. The Launch Edition adds unique packaging and a surprise \"Lucky Blind Box\" collectible figure.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti GPU (GB203) on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, featuring 8960 CUDA cores, 70 ray tracing cores, and 280 Tensor cores. It\'s paired with 16GB of GDDR7 memory on a 256-bit bus at 28 Gbps, delivering roughly 896 GB/s of memory bandwidth. As MSI\'s Super Overclocked (SOC) flagship variant, it ships with a 2588 MHz boost clock — a 5.5% jump over NVIDIA\'s 2452 MHz reference spec — reaching up to 2602 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode.</p><p>Within MSI\'s RTX 5070 Ti lineup, which spans Ventus, Gaming Trio, Vanguard, Inspire, and Shadow series, the Vanguard line sits just below MSI\'s premium Suprim series, sharing a similarly refined build quality but with a darker aesthetic, more RGB accenting, and its own factory clock tuning. The SOC designation marks this as the highest factory-overclocked model in the Vanguard range, while the Launch Edition designation specifically adds a limited-run bundle: a \"Lucky\" figurine blind box containing one of ten collectible designs (including a rare secret edition) tied to MSI\'s \"Lucky Around the World\" launch campaign — the underlying card and cooling hardware are otherwise identical to the standard Vanguard SOC.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution, along with NVIDIA Reflex 2 for reduced input latency. Display output is upgraded to DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting resolutions up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>The Vanguard series carries MSI\'s premium design language, with aerodynamic edges, carbon fiber-inspired shroud patterns, and generous RGB lighting throughout. Cooling comes from MSI\'s substantial Hyper Frozr thermal design — a sizeable 357 x 151 x 66mm cooler featuring triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades, a large integrated vapor chamber paired with square-shaped core pipes for enhanced heat dissipation, and a metal backplate for structural reinforcement. A physical Gaming/Silent mode switch along the card\'s edge lets users toggle between BIOS profiles, with Silent mode using a gentler fan curve for quieter operation. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring, RGB customization, and tuning, plus MSI Afterburner for advanced overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (GB203-200)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8960 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>70</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>280</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2588 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode SOC), up to 2602 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>28 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~896 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>750W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>357 x 151 x 66 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x STORMFORCE fans</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Control</td><td>Physical Gaming/Silent BIOS switch</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>Hyper Frozr Thermal Design — vapor chamber, square core pipes, metal backplate</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Design Language</td><td>Carbon fiber-inspired shroud, extensive RGB</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Special Edition</td><td>Launch Edition packaging + Lucky Blind Box figurine (1 of 10 designs)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center (Gaming/Silent mode), MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', 'Graphics Card', 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/ZqS6NnHP0VACsnBMN3hnsgfOTnQxyUVr9iDETZDJ.webp', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 13:21:08', '2026-07-12 13:21:08', 'MSI RTX 5070 Ti 16G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition | 16GB GDDR7 GPU', 'Get the MSI GeForce RTX 5070 Ti 16G Vanguard SOC Launch Edition — 16GB GDDR7, Hyper Frozr cooling, DLSS 4, up to 2602 MHz boost, includes Lucky Blind Box. Buy now!', 'MSI RTX 5070 Ti Vanguard SOC, Vanguard La