(1250, 'MSI GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER 16G VENTUS 3X OC GDDR6X Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER 16G Ventus 3X OC delivers high-end 4K gaming and creative performance in MSI\'s clean, no-frills Ventus design. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, it offers 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 10240 CUDA cores, and boost clocks up to 2595 MHz, cooled by triple TORX Fan 4.0 blades — a strong value pick among RTX 4080 SUPER options for gamers who want performance without a premium price tag.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-4080-super-16g-ventus-3x-oc-gddr6x-graphics-card-1783862620', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER 16G Ventus 3X OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER GPU, delivering 10240 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR6X memory across a 256-bit bus at 23 Gbps. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2580 MHz boost clock, reaching up to 2595 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode, and is capable of roughly 53 TFLOPS of FP32 compute performance.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports ray tracing, DLSS 3 with AI-accelerated frame generation, and NVIDIA Reflex for reduced input latency, along with full DirectX 12 Ultimate and OpenGL 4.6 support. Owners consistently note strong 1440p and 4K performance with cool operating temperatures, making it a dependable choice for demanding modern titles.</p><p>As MSI\'s entry point into the RTX 4080 SUPER lineup, the Ventus 3X OC keeps a clean, understated design without the RGB lighting or premium finishes found on pricier variants like the Gaming X Slim or Expert — a deliberate trade-off that keeps the price more accessible while retaining the same core GPU performance. Cooling comes from triple TORX Fan 4.0 blades working in pairs for focused, high-pressure airflow, complemented by Airflow Control technology that directs air where it\'s needed most. The card includes a bundled anti-sag bracket to support its weight in the case, and is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p>', '<p>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G EXPERT GDDR6X Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Searched the web</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Great, I have solid data on this distinctive line. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G EXPERT</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Expert | 16GB GDDR6X Graphics Card</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Get the MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Expert — 16GB GDDR6X, push-pull airflow cooling, DLSS 3, up to 2685 MHz boost, premium aluminum design. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super Expert, Expert series graphics card, RTX 4070 Ti Super 16GB, MSI RTX 4070 Ti Super price, push-pull airflow GPU, DLSS 3 graphics card, Ada Lovelace GPU, premium aluminum GPU, RTX 4070 Ti Super specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Expert brings a distinctive push-pull airflow cooling system and premium aluminum alloy casing to MSI\'s high-end lineup. Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, it offers 16GB of GDDR6X memory, 8448 CUDA cores, and one of the highest factory boost clocks in the RTX 4070 Ti SUPER family at up to 2685 MHz — combining refined looks with serious performance for gamers and creators.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER 16G Expert is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER GPU, delivering 8448 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR6X memory across a 256-bit bus at 21 Gbps. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2670 MHz boost clock, reaching up to 2685 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode, matching the top clocks found on MSI\'s Gaming X Slim variant.</p><p>Part of MSI\'s Expert series, this card is built around a distinctive push-pull airflow system, where two sets of fans work together — one pushing cool air into the heatsink while the other pulls hot air away — for improved cooling efficiency and reduced heat buildup. A patented fan design gives the card a distinctive appearance while further enhancing heat dissipation. The card\'s aluminum alloy casing adds durability and stability while giving it a refined, premium look that sets it apart from MSI\'s standard gaming-branded cards.</p><p>Built on NVIDIA\'s Ada Lovelace architecture, the card supports third-gen RT Cores for fast, realistic ray tracing and fourth-gen Tensor Cores with an Optical Flow Accelerator for DLSS 3 frame generation, along with NVIDIA Reflex for reduced input latency. Cooling is further supported by a copper baseplate that captures heat from the GPU and memory modules and rapidly transfers it to core pipes, along with dual ball-bearing fans and MSI\'s ZERO FROZR feature for silent idle operation. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring and tuning, with MSI Afterburner and its OC Scanner feature available for automated, stable overclocking.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (AD103-275)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8448 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>66 (3rd Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>264 (4th Gen)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2670 MHz (up to 2685 MHz Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td