rical protection under sustained heavy loads. This makes it a strong pick for extended gaming sessions, streaming, or demanding creative workloads where consistent power delivery matters.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution for major gains in frame rate and image quality, alongside NVIDIA Reflex 2 for reduced input latency. Display connectivity includes DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 4K at 480Hz or 8K at 120Hz with DSC, VRR, and HDR.</p><p>As part of MSI\'s flagship Gaming Trio line, the card carries a fierce, sharp-edged design with diffused LED lighting and a dragon totem motif. Cooling comes from MSI\'s TRI FROZR 4 thermal design, featuring triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades and double ball bearings for durability, a nickel-plated copper baseplate for fast heat capture, square-profile core pipes running the full length of the board, and an Airflow Control radiator with Antegrade 2.0 fins to reduce turbulence. A perforated metal backplate reinforces the chassis while helping release trapped heat, and a bundled support bracket helps prevent GPU sag. The card is managed through MSI Center\'s Gaming and Silent modes plus MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (GB203)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8960 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>280</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2572 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode), up to 2580 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Cente