ard\'s edge lets users toggle between BIOS profiles, with Silent mode using a gentler fan curve for quieter operation. The card is managed through MSI Center for real-time monitoring, RGB customization, and tuning, plus MSI Afterburner for advanced overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (GB203-200)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell, 4nm process</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>8960 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>70</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>280</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2588 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode SOC), up to 2602 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>28 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~896 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>750W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>357 x 151 x 66 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x STORMFORCE fans</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Control</td><td>Physical Gaming/Silent BIOS switch<