e for demanding modern titles.</p><p>As MSI\'s entry point into the RTX 4080 SUPER lineup, the Ventus 3X OC keeps a clean, understated design without the RGB lighting or premium finishes found on pricier variants like the Gaming X Slim or Expert — a deliberate trade-off that keeps the price more accessible while retaining the same core GPU performance. Cooling comes from triple TORX Fan 4.0 blades working in pairs for focused, high-pressure airflow, complemented by Airflow Control technology that directs air where it\'s needed most. The card includes a bundled anti-sag bracket to support its weight in the case, and is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>Ada Lovelace</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>10240 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2580 MHz (up to 2595 MHz Extreme Performance / MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Compute Performance</td><td>~53.14 TFLOPS (FP32)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR6X</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>23 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>2x DisplayPort (v1.4a), 2x HDMI (2.1a — 4K@120Hz HDR, 8K@60Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</t