(1254, 'MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G GAMING TRIO OC WHITE 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Gaming Trio OC White brings flagship-tier performance to a clean, all-white aesthetic built for style-matched builds. Powered by NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and DLSS 4, it features 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 10752 CUDA cores, and a factory-overclocked boost speed up to 2715 MHz, backed by MSI\'s TWIN FROZR 10 thermal design with triple STORMFORCE fans.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-5080-16g-gaming-trio-oc-white-16gb-gddr7-graphics-card-1783863217', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Gaming Trio OC White is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 GPU on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, delivering 10752 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR7 memory across a 256-bit bus at 30 Gbps. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2700 MHz boost clock in Gaming/Silent mode, climbing to 2715 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — matching the performance of the standard black Gaming Trio OC in a white and silver finish.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution for major gains in frame rate and image quality. The RTX 50-series\' upgraded encode/decode engine also benefits creators, supporting 4:2:2 pro-grade color, Multiview-HEVC for 3D and VR video, and AV1 Ultra High Quality mode — useful for editing high-resolution footage smoothly in Adobe Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, and similar applications. Display connectivity includes DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 8K resolution at 7680 x 4320.</p><p>As part of MSI\'s flagship Gaming Trio line, this card carries the same fierce, sharp-edged design as the standard model, reworked in a crisp white and silver colorway for builds that favor a brighter aesthetic. Cooling comes from MSI\'s newest TWIN FROZR 10 thermal design, featuring triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades for high airflow and low noise, a nickel-plated copper baseplate for fast heat capture, square-profile core pipes for maximum GPU contact, and Wave-Curved 3.0 fin geometry to optimize airflow in low-flow zones. A reinforcing metal backplate with vents and thermal pads rounds out the cooling package. The card includes Dual BIOS, letting users choose between a full-performance Gaming mode or a quieter Silent mode, and is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p>', '<p>CategoryFeatureSpecification<strong>Core</strong>GPUNVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080CoreArchitectureNVIDIA BlackwellCoreCUDA Cores10752 UnitsCoreBoost Clock2700 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode), up to 2715 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)<strong>Memory</strong>Memory Size16GB GDDR7MemoryMemory Bus256-bitMemoryMemory Speed30 Gbps<strong>Connectivity</strong>InterfacePCI Express Gen 5ConnectivityDisplay Outputs3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)ConnectivityMax Digital Resolution7680 x 4320 (8K)ConnectivityMax Displays4ConnectivityHDCP SupportYesConnectivityG-SYNC SupportYes<strong>Power</strong>Power Connector1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)PowerPower Consumption360 WPowerRecommended PSU750W and above<strong>Physical</strong>Card Dimensions338 mm lengthPhysicalColorWhite / SilverPhysicalFans3x STORMFORCE fans<strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong>Cooling SystemTWIN FROZR 10, nickel-plated copper baseplate, square core pipes, Wave-Curved 3.0Cooling &amp; DesignBackplateReinforcing metal backplate with vents and thermal padsCooling &amp; DesignSpecial FeaturesDual BIOS (Gaming/Silent mode)<strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong>DLSSDLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)Software &amp; TechLatency TechNVIDIA Reflex 2Software &amp; TechSoftware SuiteMSI Center (Gaming/Silent mode), MSI Afterburner</p>', 'Graphics Card', 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/C9kW0IG7TQZcGWe80M3uoPeuiWkG7