(1256, 'MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G GAMING TRIO OC WHITE 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Gaming Trio OC White brings flagship-tier performance to a clean, all-white aesthetic built for style-matched builds. Powered by NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and DLSS 4, it features 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 10752 CUDA cores, and a factory-overclocked boost speed up to 2715 MHz, backed by MSI\'s TWIN FROZR 10 thermal design with triple STORMFORCE fans.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-5080-16g-gaming-trio-oc-white-16gb-gddr7-graphics-card-1783863447', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Gaming Trio OC White is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 GPU on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, delivering 10752 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR7 memory across a 256-bit bus at 30 Gbps. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2700 MHz boost clock in Gaming/Silent mode, climbing to 2715 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode — matching the performance of the standard black Gaming Trio OC in a white and silver finish.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution for major gains in frame rate and image quality. The RTX 50-series\' upgraded encode/decode engine also benefits creators, supporting 4:2:2 pro-grade color, Multiview-HEVC for 3D and VR video, and AV1 Ultra High Quality mode — useful for editing high-resolution footage smoothly in Adobe Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, and similar applications. Display connectivity includes DisplayPort 2.1b and HDMI 2.1b, supporting up to 8K resolution at 7680 x 4320.</p><p>As part of MSI\'s flagship Gaming Trio line, this card carries the same fierce, sharp-edged design as the standard model, reworked in a crisp white and silver colorway for builds that favor a brighter aesthetic. Cooling comes from MSI\'s newest TWIN FROZR 10 thermal design, featuring triple STORMFORCE fans with seven claw-textured blades for high airflow and low noise, a nickel-plated copper baseplate for fast heat capture, square-profile core pipes for maximum GPU contact, and Wave-Curved 3.0 fin geometry to optimize airflow in low-flow zones. A reinforcing metal backplate with vents and thermal pads rounds out the cooling package. The card includes Dual BIOS, letting users choose between a full-performance Gaming mode or a quieter Silent mode, and is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Feature</th><th>Specification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>10752 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2700 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode), up to 2715 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>30 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320 (8K)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>360 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>750W and above</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>338 mm length</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Color</td><td>White / Silver</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x STORMFORCE fans</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>TWIN FROZR 10, nickel-plated copper baseplate, square core pipes, Wave-Curved 3.0</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Backplate</td><td>Reinforcing metal backplate with vents and thermal pads</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Special Features</td><td>Dual BIOS (Gaming/Silent mode)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center (Gaming/Silent mode), MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', NULL, 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/RFgGoIg2uPhrk67lvPScbqfiQFFm8u1rWPgLOYmR.webp', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 13:37:27', '2026-07-12 13:37:27', 'MSI RTX 5080 16G Gaming Trio OC White | 16GB GDDR7 GPU', 'Shop the MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Gaming Trio OC White — 16GB GDDR7, TWIN FROZR 10 cooling, DLSS 4, up to 2715 MHz boost clock, sleek white design. Buy now!', 'MSI RTX 5080 Gaming Trio OC White, RTX 5080 white graphics card, RTX 5080 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5080 price, TWIN FROZR 10 GPU, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, white gaming GPU, RTX 5080 specs, MSI graphics card 2026', NULL, 14, NULL, NULL),
(1257, 'MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G EXPERT OC 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Expert OC brings a premium, Founders Edition-inspired push-pull cooling design to NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and DLSS 4. Encased in precision die-cast aluminum alloy, it delivers 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 10752 CUDA cores, and a factory-overclocked boost speed up to 2730 MHz — a refined alternative to MSI\'s RGB-forward Gaming and Vanguard lines for gamers and creators who prefer understated, premium styling.', 'msi-geforce-rtx-5080-16g-expert-oc-16gb-gddr7-graphics-card-1783863517', '<p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Expert OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 GPU on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, delivering 10752 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR7 memory across a 256-bit bus at 30 Gbps, for roughly 960 GB/s of memory bandwidth — a substantial jump over the previous generation\'s GDDR6X. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2715 MHz boost clock, about 4% above NVIDIA\'s 2617 MHz reference spec, with MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode pushing it further to 2730 MHz. In real-world testing, the card has been shown to boost even higher than its rated spec under typical loads.</p><p>In MSI\'s graphics card hierarchy, the Expert series sits just below the premium Vanguard line and above the standard Gaming series, offering a distinct design language: rather than RGB lighting and aggressive styling, Expert cards borrow the iconic push-pull cooling concept from NVIDIA\'s own Founders Edition design, reimagined with MSI\'s own engineering and finished in a precision die-cast aluminum alloy shell for a clean, premium look with genuine structural rigidity. At 319 x 150 x 60mm, the card is larger in every dimension than the RTX 5080 Founders Edition, effectively a 3-slot-wide design, but keeps the same clean, adornment-free aesthetic apart from GeForce RTX branding and an Expert badge protecting the power connector during shipping.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution. The RTX 5080 sits at roughly 85% of the RTX 5090\'s performance at a notably lower price point, offering meaningful raster and ray tracing gains over the previous-generation RTX 4080, along with a fifth-generation NVENC encoder for efficient AV1 encoding that benefits video editors working in Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, and similar tools.</p><p>Cooling comes from MSI\'s Flow Frozr 2 thermal design, featuring a large vapor chamber affixed directly to the GPU and memory, connected to a heatsink spanning nearly the full length of the card via square-shaped Core Pipes. Dual ball-bearing STORMFORCE fans with seven blades handle push-pull airflow — the front fan blows air down directly onto the GPU and memory, while the rear fan pulls air through the heatsink in a pass-through design similar to NVIDIA\'s own reference cooler. The card also features DrMOS power circuitry and a PCB MSI describes as engineered with hardened circuits and optimized trace routing for reliability. Dual BIOS lets users toggle between full-performance Gaming mode and a quieter Silent mode, and the card is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Feature</th><th>Specification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>10752 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2715 MHz, up to 2730 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>30 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>~960 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5 x16</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320 (8K)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>360 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>850W</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>319 x 150 x 60 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Weight (Card/Package)</td><td>1898 g / 2760 g</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Build Material</td><td>Precision die-cast aluminum alloy</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>Dual ball-bearing STORMFORCE fans (push-pull)</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Included Accessories</td><td>GPU support stand, 12VHPWR to 3x 8-pin power adapter</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>Flow Frozr 2 — vapor chamber, square Core Pipes, push-pull dual-fan airflow</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Power Delivery</td><td>DrMOS circuitry, hardened PCB with optimized trace routing</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Special Features</td><td>Dual BIOS (Gaming/Silent mode)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center, MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', NULL, 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/0Zee4LN52W3uPcbnEYvKx1qKd4mRowlCeBgKEPXo.webp', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 13:38:37', '2026-07-12 13:38:37', 'MSI RTX 5080 16G Expert OC | 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'Get the MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Expert OC — 16GB GDDR7, push-pull Flow Frozr 2 cooling, DLSS 4, up to 2730 MHz boost, premium die-cast aluminum. Buy now!', 'vMSI RTX 5080 Expert OC, Expert series graphics card, RTX 5080 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5080 price, push-pull airflow GPU, Flow Frozr 2 cooling, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, RTX 5080 specs, MSI graphics card 2026', NULL, 14, NULL, NULL);
