ling, DLSS 4, up to 2730 MHz boost, premium die-cast aluminum. Buy now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5080 Expert OC, Expert series graphics card, RTX 5080 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5080 price, push-pull airflow GPU, Flow Frozr 2 cooling, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, RTX 5080 specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Expert OC brings a premium, Founders Edition-inspired push-pull cooling design to NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture and DLSS 4. Encased in precision die-cast aluminum alloy, it delivers 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 10752 CUDA cores, and a factory-overclocked boost speed up to 2730 MHz — a refined alternative to MSI\'s RGB-forward Gaming and Vanguard lines for gamers and creators who prefer understated, premium styling.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Expert OC is powered by the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 GPU on NVIDIA\'s Blackwell architecture, delivering 10752 CUDA cores alongside 16GB of GDDR7 memory across a 256-bit bus at 30 Gbps, for roughly 960 GB/s of memory bandwidth — a substantial jump over the previous generation\'s GDDR6X. The card ships factory-overclocked with a 2715 MHz boost clock, about 4% above NVIDIA\'s 2617 MHz reference spec, with MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode pushing it further to 2730 MHz. In real-world testing, the card has been shown to boost even higher than its rated spec under typical loads.</p><p>In MSI\'s graphics card hierarchy, the Expert series sits just below the premium Vanguard line and above the standard Gaming series, offering a distinct design language: rather than RGB lighting and aggressive styling, Expert cards borrow the iconic push-pull cooling concept from NVIDIA\'s own Founders Edition design, reimagined with MSI\'s own engineering and finished in a precision die-cast aluminum alloy shell for a clean, premium look with genuine structural rigidity. At 319 x 150 x 60mm, the card is larger in every dimension than the RTX 5080 Founders Edition, effectively a 3-slot-wide design, but keeps the same clean, adornment-free aesthetic apart from GeForce RTX branding and an Expert badge protecting the power connector during shipping.</p><p>Blackwell brings fourth-gen RT Cores and fifth-gen Tensor Cores to the table, enabling DLSS 4 with Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution. The RTX 5080 sits at roughly 85% of the RTX 5090\'s performance at a notably lower price point, offering meaningful raster and ray tracing gains over the previous-generation RTX 4080, along with a fifth-generation NVENC encoder for efficient AV1 encoding that benefits video editors working in Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, and similar tools.</p><p>Cooling comes from MSI\'s Flow Frozr 2 thermal design, featuring a large vapor chamber affixed directly to the GPU and memory, connected to a heatsink spanning nearly the full length of the card via square-shaped Core Pipes. Dual ball-bearing STORMFORCE fans with seven blades handle push-pull airflow — the front fan blows air down directly onto the GPU and memory, while the rear fan pulls air through the heatsink in a pass-through design similar to NVIDIA\'s own reference cooler. The card also features DrMOS power circuitry and a PCB MSI describes as engineered with hardened circuits and optimized trace routing for reliability. Dual BIOS lets users toggle between full-performance Gaming mode and a quieter Silent mode, and the card is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</t