d>Dual BIOS (Gaming/Silent mode)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center, MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>Want this exported as a ready-to-use file (HTML, Markdown, or CSV for a specific platform)? Given how many cards we\'ve now covered, I\'d also genuinely recommend letting me build a single catalog spreadsheet — happy to do that whenever you\'re ready.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G VANGUARD SOC 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Synthesized performance benchmarks for graphics card analysis</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Synthesized performance benchmarks for graphics card analysis</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Excellent, detailed data including a full TechPowerUp review. Here\'s the complete SEO and product listing content for the <strong>MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G VANGUARD SOC</strong>:</p><h3><strong>Meta Title</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5080 16G Vanguard SOC | 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card</p><h3><strong>Meta Description</strong></h3><p>Buy the MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Vanguard SOC — 16GB GDDR7, Hyper Frozr vapor chamber cooling, DLSS 4, up to 2745 MHz boost clock. Shop now!</p><h3><strong>Meta Keywords</strong></h3><p>MSI RTX 5080 Vanguard SOC, Vanguard series graphics card, RTX 5080 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5080 price, Hyper Frozr cooling, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, vapor chamber GPU, RTX 5080 specs, MSI graphics card 2026</p><h3><strong>Short Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Vanguard SOC combines MSI\'s premium Vanguard design language with a heavily factory-overclocked RTX 5080, positioned between MSI\'s halo-tier Suprim line and its Gaming X series. It delivers 16GB of GDDR7 memory, 10752 CUDA cores, and a boost clock up to 2745 MHz, cooled by MSI\'s Hyper Frozr thermal design with vapor chamber technology and triple STORMFORCE fans — built for serious 4K gaming and creative performance.</p><h3><strong>Long Description</strong></h3><p>The MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Vanguard SOC is powered by a fully unlocked NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 GPU (GB203), enabling all 84 streaming multiprocessors for 10752 CUDA cores, 336 Tensor cores, 84 RT cores, and the chip\'s full 64MB of on-die L2 cache. It\'s paired with 16GB of GDDR7 memory on a 256-bit bus running at 30 Gbps, delivering 960 GB/s of memory bandwidth — a 34% increase over the previous-generation RTX 4080. As the \"SOC\" (Super Overclocked) variant, it ships with a 2730 MHz boost clock on both its Gaming and Silent BIOS profiles, well above NVIDIA\'s 2617 MHz reference spec, reaching up to 2745 MHz in MSI Center\'s Extreme Performance mode.</p><p>MSI\'s new Vanguard line sits between its halo-tier Suprim series and its more mainstream Gaming X line, effectively serving as the successor to the retired Gaming Z series. Design-wise, it borrows titanium-gray metal alloy accents and a brushed-aluminum backplate from Suprim, alongside carbon fiber surfacing and acrylic RGB LED diffusers reminiscent of Gaming X — resulting in a distinctive, premium look with generous RGB lighting.</p><p>Blackwell\'s display engine implements DisplayPort 2.1b with UHBR20 on all ports, enabling 8K high-refresh-rate output over a single cable when paired with DSC, and dual NVDEC/NVENC video accelerators support 4:2:2 color formats for both AV1 and HEVC encoding. DLSS 4 brings Multi Frame Generation, enhanced Ray Reconstruction, and Super Resolution, all accelerated by fifth-gen Tensor Cores, alongside NVIDIA Reflex 2 for reduced input latency.</p><p>Cooling comes from MSI\'s Hyper Frozr thermal design, borrowing cooling innovations from the Suprim series: a vapor chamber plate makes direct contact with the GPU and memory, transferring heat to a cluster of flattened, cuboidal heat pipes for maximum contact with the vapor chamber, then spreading it across a large aluminum fin stack with wavy edges designed to increase turbulence for better heat dissipation. Triple STORMFORCE fans with double ball bearings handle airflow — the same fans found on MSI\'s flagship Suprim RTX 5080. Dual BIOS lets users choose between full-performance Gaming mode and a quieter Silent mode, and the card is managed through MSI Center and MSI Afterburner for real-time monitoring, tuning, and overclocking control.</p><h3><strong>Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core</strong></td><td>GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 (GB203, fully unlocked)</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Architecture</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>10752 Units</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Tensor Cores</td><td>336</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Ray Tracing Cores</td><td>84</td></tr><tr><td>Core</td><td>Boost Clock</td><td>2730 MHz (Gaming/Silent Mode SOC), up to 2745 MHz Extreme Performance (MSI Center)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory</strong></td><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bus</td><td>256-bit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>30 Gbps</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>960 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>Interface</td><td>PCI Express Gen 5</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Display Outputs</td><td>3x DisplayPort (v2.1b, UHBR20), 1x HDMI (2.1b — up to 4K@480Hz or 8K@120Hz with DSC, VRR, HDR)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Digital Resolution</td><td>7680 x 4320 (8K)</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Max Displays</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>HDCP Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>G-SYNC Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power</strong></td><td>Power Connector</td><td>1x 16-pin (12VHPWR)</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Power Consumption</td><td>360 W</td></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td>Recommended PSU</td><td>850W</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>Card Dimensions</td><td>357 mm length</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Color</td><td>Black / Silver with RGB accents</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Fans</td><td>3x STORMFORCE fans (double ball bearing)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cooling &amp; Design</strong></td><td>Cooling System</td><td>Hyper Frozr — vapor chamber, cuboidal heat pipes, wavy-edge aluminum fin stack</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Design Language</td><td>Titanium-gray metal alloy accents, carbon fiber surfacing, RGB LED diffusers</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling &amp; Design</td><td>Special Features</td><td>Dual BIOS (Gaming/Silent mode)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Software &amp; Tech</strong></td><td>DLSS</td><td>DLSS 4 (Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Super Resolution)</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Latency Tech</td><td>NVIDIA Reflex 2</td></tr><tr><td>Software &amp; Tech</td><td>Software Suite</td><td>MSI Center (Gaming/Silent mode), MSI Afterburner</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', 'Graphics Card', 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/iSdU0z6Bfk2IPN7Cj08WzH91OHTPoIxkT9MYmQte.webp', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 13:39:34', '2026-07-12 13:39:34', 'MSI RTX 5080 16G Vanguard SOC | 16GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'Buy the MSI GeForce RTX 5080 16G Vanguard SOC — 16GB GDDR7, Hyper Frozr vapor chamber cooling, DLSS 4, up to 2745 MHz boost clock. Shop now!', 'MSI RTX 5080 Vanguard SOC, Vanguard series graphics card, RTX 5080 16GB GDDR7, MSI RTX 5080 price, Hyper Frozr cooling, DLSS 4 graphics card, Blackwell architecture GPU, vapor chamber GPU, RTX 5080 specs, MSI graphics card 2026', NULL, 14, NULL, NULL);
