(1323, 'ASUS Dual GeForce RTX 4060 Ti EVO OC Edition 16GB GDDR6 Graphics Card', 'The ASUS Dual GeForce RTX 4060 Ti EVO OC Edition 16GB GDDR6 blends high-tier rendering power with broad system chassis compatibility. Built on the ultra-efficient NVIDIA Ada Lovelace architecture, it sports a massive 16GB VRAM buffer engineered to handle high-resolution texture streaming, intense 3D layouts, and advanced AI workflows. Featuring twin specialized Axial-tech fans, an armor-grade structural protective backplate, and an intelligent 0dB silent profile, this 2.5-slot card easily integrates into compact and mid-tower builds.', 'asus-dual-geforce-rtx-4060-ti-evo-oc-edition-16gb-gddr6-graphics-card-1783883651', '<p>The ASUS Dual GeForce RTX 4060 Ti EVO OC Edition 16GB GDDR6 delivers performance-focused engineering designed to eliminate data bottlenecks for modern creators and competitive gamers. By deploying an expansive 16GB GDDR6 memory configuration, this card completely eliminates high-resolution texture dropouts, providing fluid multi-layer timelines in Premiere Pro, fast asset compiling in Blender, and massive headroom for demanding generative AI frameworks. Driven by the 5nm NVIDIA Ada Lovelace framework, it uses 4th Generation Tensor Cores to output up to 361 AI TOPS of neural acceleration—scaling frame rates up to 4x via DLSS 3 Frame Generation compared to traditional brute-force computing.</p><p>To effortlessly manage its factory-overclocked boost clock speeds up to 2625 MHz, the EVO series implements an optimized dual-fan thermal assembly. Twin flagship Axial-tech fans feature scaled-down center hubs to accommodate longer blades, bounded by an outer barrier ring that actively drives dense, high-pressure downward airflow directly through the aluminum heatsink fins. The inclusion of premium dual ball fan bearings effectively doubles operational lifetimes compared to conventional sleeve bearing variants. Fully assembled using precision Auto-Extreme automated soldering to minimize structural stress, and rounded out with a protective backplate, rigid 304 stainless steel mounting bracket, and a hardware Dual BIOS toggle, it serves as an uncompromising centerpiece for high-tier desktop systems.</p><h2>&nbsp;</h2>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification Details</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Graphics Processor</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Ti (AD106)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>4,352 Units</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Engine Clock (Default Mode)</td><td>Boost Clock: 2595 MHz</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Engine Clock (OC Mode)</td><td>Boost Clock: 2625 MHz</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>AI Computing Performance</td><td>361 AI TOPS</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Video Memory Configuration</td><td>16GB GDDR6</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Clock Speed</td><td>18 Gbps (Effective)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Interface Width</td><td>128-bit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Bus Interface</td><td>PCI Express 4.0 x8 (Physical x16 form factor)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>Digital Max Resolution</td><td>$7680 \\times 4320$ (8K Ultra HD)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>Multi-Display Capability</td><td>Quad Display (Supports up to 4 concurrent monitors)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>HDCP Compliant</td><td>Yes (Version 2.3)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>HDMI Interface</td><td>1x Native HDMI 2.1a</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>DisplayPort Interface</td><td>3x Native DisplayPort 1.4a</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></t