(1358, 'Zotac Gaming GeForce GTX 1650 AMP 4GB GDDR6 Graphics Card', 'The ZOTAC GAMING GeForce GTX 1650 AMP 4GB GDDR6 brings super-compact, factory-overclocked performance to entry-tier gaming rigs and space-constrained desktop layouts. Built on the efficient NVIDIA Turing architecture, it features a 4GB buffer of fast GDDR6 memory operating over a 128-bit bus. Running with a highly efficient 75W maximum power draw, its short 16.2 cm dual-slot footprint fits seamlessly into nearly any standard or small-form-factor chassis, while a custom 70mm dual-fan layout provides excellent, quiet thermal performance without demanding extensive power supply overhead.', 'zotac-gaming-geforce-gtx-1650-amp-4gb-gddr6-graphics-card-1783887052', '<p>The ZOTAC GAMING GeForce GTX 1650 AMP 4GB GDDR6 balances space-saving hardware design with reliable entry-level gaming muscle, tailoring it perfectly for budget-conscious builders and everyday productivity systems. Grounded on the 12nm NVIDIA Turing framework, this GPU features an upgraded memory pipeline over its legacy GDDR5 counterparts, utilizing 896 processing CUDA cores coupled with ultra-fast GDDR6 video memory running at a fast 12 Gbps. This boost in memory bandwidth effectively minimizes frame stuttering and high-resolution texture delivery drops, enabling casual esports competitors and digital content creators to maintain fluid, stutter-free performance at high-setting 1080p resolutions. Out of the box, it arrives factory-overclocked to an aggressive 1650 MHz engine boost clock for out-of-the-box system responsiveness.</p><p>True to ZOTAC’s engineering focus on compact system building, the GTX 1650 AMP features a highly compatible dual-slot layout measuring just 16.2 cm in total length, maximizing internal chassis airflow even inside crowded configurations. Operating at a low 75W total board power profile, it safely utilizes a standard power draw matrix that dramatically simplifies power distribution. Thermal management is driven by a specialized 70mm dual-fan configuration paired with a high-density aluminum block heatsink that quickly draws heat away from the core components. Finished with native triple simultaneous display capabilities via independent HDMI, DisplayPort, and Dual-Link DVI-D connectivity, it acts as a robust, highly versatile engine for compact computing rigs.</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification Details</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Graphics Processor</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>896 Units</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Engine Clock (Boost Mode)</td><td>1650 MHz (Factory Overclocked)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Architecture Framework</td><td>NVIDIA Turing Architecture</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Video Memory Configuration</td><td>4GB GDDR6</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Clock Speed</td><td>12.0 Gbps (Effective)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Interface Width</td><td>128-bit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>192 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Bus Standard / Interface</td><td>PCI Express 3.0 x16</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>Digital Max Resolution</td><td>$7680 \\times 4320$ (8K Ultra HD Support)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>Maximum Display Connections</td><td>Triple Display Support (Up to 3 concurrent monitors)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>HDCP Version Support</td><td>Yes (Version 2.2)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>HDMI Interface</td><td>1x Native HDMI 2.0b (Supports 4K @ 60Hz)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>DisplayPort Interface</td><td>1x Native DisplayPort 1.4</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>DVI Interface</td><td>1x Dual-Link DVI-D</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></td><td>Estimated Power Draw (TDP)</td><td>75W Max Power Consumption</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></td><td>Recommended System PSU</td><td>350W</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></td><td>External Power Connectors</td><td>None / Slot Powered</td></tr><tr><td><strong>API Support</strong></td><td>DirectX Support</td><td>DirectX 12 API (Feature Level 12_1)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>API Support</strong></td><td>OpenGL Support</td><td>OpenGL 4.6</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical Specs</strong></td><td>Dimensions (L x W x H)</td><td>162.4 x 111.15 x 37.1 mm (6.39 x 4.38 x 1.46 inches)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical Specs</strong></td><td>Form Factor Slot Width</td><td>Dual-Slot Profile (Super Compact layout)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical Specs</strong></td><td>Cooling Engineering</td><td>Dual 70mm Cooling Fans, Vented Aluminum Heatsink</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Warranty</strong></td><td>Product Warranty</td><td>3 Years Standard + 2 Years Extended Warranty (Upon Online Registration)</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', 'Graphics Card', 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/WgvXYnv8UaUOmAMWhQiJu5jjls1rZW3M0DSB7PF1.jpg', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 20:10:52', '2026-07-12 20:10:52', 'Meta Title: ZOTAC GAMING GeForce GTX 1650 AMP 4GB GDDR6 Graphics Card', 'Meta Description: Buy the factory-overclocked ZOTAC GAMING GeForce GTX 1650 AMP 4GB GDDR6. Features 896 CUDA cores, dual 70mm fans, a 75W low power profile, and triple display support.', 'Keywords: Zotac GTX 1650 AMP GDDR6 price, ZT-T16520D-10L, GeForce GTX 1650 4GB, NVIDIA Turing graphics card, compact dual-fan GPU, entry level gaming PC build Bangladesh', NULL, 141, NULL, NULL),
(1359, 'ZOTAC GAMING GeForce RTX 5090 SOLID 32GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'The ZOTAC GAMING GeForce RTX 5090 SOLID 32GB GDDR7 represents the absolute zenith of consumer graphics processing, engineered for no-frills, all-action flagship desktop performance. Powered by the groundbreaking NVIDIA Blackwell architecture, it combines a monumental 32GB buffer of next-generation GDDR7 memory across an ultra-wide 512-bit data bus. Housed within a massive, heavy-duty 3.5-slot industrial enclosure, this powerhouse utilizes an advanced IceStorm 3.0 thermal layout with a 34% larger vapor chamber, high-pressure 100mm BladeLink triple fans, a hardware-level 12V-2x6 Power Safety Light, and structural metal reinforcement to easily dominate extreme local AI development and uncompromising 8K rendering environments.', 'zotac-gaming-geforce-rtx-5090-solid-32gb-gddr7-graphics-card-1783887201', '<p>The ZOTAC GAMING GeForce RTX 5090 SOLID 32GB GDDR7 fuses raw computational muscle with an industrial-grade structural design built for maximum physical rigidity and cooling supremacy. Grounded on the cutting-edge 5nm NVIDIA Blackwell architecture, this flagship graphics accelerator features a mind-boggling array of 21,760 high-performance CUDA cores alongside 5th Generation Tensor Cores and 4th Generation Ray Tracing Cores. These hardware arrays completely revolutionize neural computing workflows, driving real-time ray-traced ambient path tracing across heavy geometry, multiplying frame outputs via NVIDIA DLSS 4 Multi Frame Generation, and slashing system latency with NVIDIA Reflex 2. Operating at a screaming 2407 MHz boost engine clock right out of the box, it processes ultra-complex real-time workloads with absolute fluid stability.</p><p>What elevates the SOLID variant past standard hardware is its massive memory subsystem and heavy-duty reliability. Outfitted with 32GB of ultra-fast next-gen GDDR7 memory running at an effective 28 Gbps speed over a 512-bit bus, it unleashes an astronomical 1.79 TB/s of bandwidth. This eliminates texture streaming limits, allowing modern digital creators, data science engineers, and AI developers to fluidly process memory-intensive generative AI datasets, massive local large-language models (LLMs), and multi-layered 8K rendering pipelines without a hint of bottlenecking.</p><p>Thermal mastery sits at the absolute core of the SOLID framework. The card implements a large 3.5-slot cooling matrix deploying ZOTAC\'s upgraded IceStorm 3.0 advanced cooling system, which integrates a 34% larger industrial vapor chamber to directly sweep heat away from the core components. Airflow is forcefully driven by triple 100mm BladeLink axial fans designed to maximize downward air pressure, while intelligent FREEZE Fan Stop technology completely silences all fan rotation during low-load tasks to eliminate ambient noise entirely. Structurally, an integrated all-metal reinforced mid-frame combines with a die-cast metal backplate to eliminate PCB flex entirely under the immense weight of the card. Completed with a diagnostic 12V-2x6 Power Safety Light that immediately alerts users to improperly seated power cables, future-proof DisplayPort 2.1b connectivity with UHBR20 support, and premium SPECTRA 2.0 ARGB lighting accents, it stands as the ultimate future-proof engine for tier-one custom desktop environments.</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification Details</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Graphics Processor</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (Blackwell)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>21,760 Units</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Engine Clock (Boost Mode)</td><td>2407 MHz</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Architecture Framework</td><td>NVIDIA Blackwell Architecture</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Ray Tracing / Tensor Architecture</td><td>4th Gen RT Cores (170) &amp; 5th Gen Tensor Cores (680)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Video Memory Configuration</td><td>32GB GDDR7</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>28 Gbps (Effective)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Interface Width</td><td>512-bit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>1,792 GB/s (1.79 TB/s)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Bus Standard / Interface</td><td>PCI Express 5.0 x16</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>Digital Max Resolution</td><td>$7680 \\times 4320$ (Up to 4K 480Hz or 8K 165Hz with DSC)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>Maximum Display Connections</td><td>Quad Display Support (Up to 4 concurrent monitors)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>HDCP Version Support</td><td>Yes (Version 2.3)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>HDMI Interface</td><td>1x Native HDMI 2.1b (Supports 4K 480Hz HDR / 8K 120Hz HDR, VRR)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>DisplayPort Interface</td><td>3x Native DisplayPort 2.1b with UHBR20</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></td><td>Estimated Power Draw (TDP)</td><td>575W Max Power Consumption</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></td><td>Recommended System PSU</td><td>1000W</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></td><td>External Power Connectors</td><td>1x 12V-2x6 / 12VHPWR Power Input Cable</td></tr><tr><td><strong>API Support</strong></td><td>DirectX Support</td><td>DirectX 12 Ultimate (Feature Level 12_2)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>API Support</strong></td><td>OpenGL Support</td><td>OpenGL 4.6</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical Specs</strong></td><td>Dimensions (L x W x H)</td><td>329.7 x 137.8 x 67.8 mm (13.0 x 5.4 x 2.7 inches)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical Specs</strong></td><td>Form Factor Slot Width</td><td>3.5-Slot Profile (Requires massive chassis clearance)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical Specs</strong></td><td>Cooling Engineering</td><td>IceStorm 3.0, 34% Larger Vapor Chamber, Triple 100mm BladeLink Fans</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Aesthetics / Structural</strong></td><td>Flagship Build Enhancements</td><td>Reinforced Metal Mid-Frame, Metal Die-cast Backplate, 12V-2x6 Safety Light, SPECTRA 2.0 RGB</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Warranty</strong></td><td>Product Warranty</td><td>3 Years Standard + 2 Years Extended Brand Warranty (Upon Registration)</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', 'Graphics Card', 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/FGAemk49p1vtkKHB37ku5hI4I2QKDfSmmoeLMKm5.webp', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 20:13:21', '2026-07-12 20:13:21', 'Meta Title: ZOTAC GAMING GeForce RTX 5090 SOLID 32GB GDDR7 Graphics Card', 'Meta Description: Buy the ultimate ZOTAC GAMING GeForce RTX 5090 SOLID 32GB. Powered by NVIDIA Blackwell architecture, featuring a massive 512-bit bus, IceStorm 3.0, and DLSS 4.', 'Keywords: Zotac RTX 5090 SOLID price, ZT-B50900D-10P, GeForce RTX 5090 32GB GDDR7, NVIDIA Blackwell GPU, DLSS 4 graphics card, flagship 8K gaming GPU Bangladesh', NULL, 141, NULL, NULL),
(1360, 'ZOTAC GeForce GT 1030 Low Profile 2GB GDDR5 Graphics Card', 'The ZOTAC GeForce GT 1030 Low Profile 2GB GDDR5 brings compact efficiency and essential multimedia acceleration to small-form-factor (SFF) home theater PCs (HTPCs) and low-profile office desktops. Powered by NVIDIA’s highly efficient Pascal architecture, it packs a 2GB buffer of GDDR5 memory running across a 64-bit bus. Operating at a highly conservative 30W maximum board draw, this single-slot card draws all its power directly from the PCIe slot—eliminating external power cables completely while delivering smooth 4K video playback and everyday entry-level computing tasks.', 'zotac-geforce-gt-1030-low-profile-2gb-gddr5-graphics-card-1783887268', '<h3>Long Description</h3><p>The ZOTAC GeForce GT 1030 Low Profile 2GB GDDR5 delivers space-saving system integration and reliable graphics acceleration tailored specifically for home entertainment centers, workspace upgrades, and legacy desktop enhancements. Built on the 14nm NVIDIA Pascal architecture framework, this graphics processor utilizes 384 CUDA cores paired with high-bandwidth GDDR5 video memory running at 6.0 GHz. This configuration provides a massive efficiency and bandwidth advantage over lower-tier SDDR4 variants, eliminating severe rendering bottlenecks to enable buttery-smooth 4K video streaming, high-definition video playback, and basic entry-tier esports gaming at stable frame rates.</p><p>What makes this low-profile component uniquely versatile is its highly optimized space layout and low thermal fingerprint. Measuring just 17.2 cm in length and sitting at a slim single-slot depth, the card slips cleanly into even the tightest mini-ITX setups and slimline business desktops. Operating at a peak power draw of only 30W, it removes the need for any complex power distribution or multi-pin PCIe cables from your power supply. Thermally, a compact custom heatsink and specialized cooling fan actively manage heat while maintaining a quiet acoustic footprint inside your chassis. Outfitted with independent HDMI 2.0b and single-link DVI-D outputs, it readily supports multi-monitor workspaces and modern 4K digital displays.</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification Details</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Graphics Processor</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce GT 1030 (GP108-300-A1)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>384 Units</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Engine Clock (Base Mode)</td><td>1227 MHz</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Engine Clock (Boost Mode)</td><td>1468 MHz</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Architecture Framework</td><td>NVIDIA Pascal Architecture</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Video Memory Configuration</td><td>2GB GDDR5</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Speed</td><td>6.0 Gbps (Effective)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Interface Width</td><td>64-bit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>48 GB/s</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</strong></td><td>Bus Standard / Interface</td><td>PCI Express 3.0 x4 (Within x16 form factor)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>Digital Max Resolution</td><td>$3840 \\times 2160$ (4K Ultra HD Support @ 60Hz via HDMI)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>Maximum Display Connections</td><td>Dual Display Support (Up to 2 concurrent monitors)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display Support</strong></td><td>HDCP Version Support</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>HDMI Interface</td><td>1x Native HDMI 2.0b (Supports 4K @ 60Hz)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td><td>DVI Interface</td><td>1x Single-Link DVI-D</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></td><td>Estimated Power Draw (TDP)</td><td>30W Max Power Consumption</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></td><td>Recommended System PSU</td><td>300W</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power Specs</strong></td><td>External Power Connectors</td><td>None (Entirely PCIe Slot Powered)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>API Support</strong></td><td>DirectX Support</td><td>DirectX 12 API (Feature Level 12_1)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>API Support</strong></td><td>OpenGL Support</td><td>OpenGL 4.5</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical Specs</strong></td><td>Dimensions (L x W x H)</td><td>172.5 x 111.15 x 16 mm (6.79 x 4.38 x 0.63 inches)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical Specs</strong></td><td>Form Factor Slot Width</td><td>Single-Slot, Low-Profile Profile (Includes low-profile bracket)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical Specs</strong></td><td>Cooling Engineering</td><td>Active Single Fan + Low Profile Aluminum Heatsink</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Warranty</strong></td><td>Product Warranty</td><td>3 Years Standard + 2 Years Extended Brand Warranty (Upon Online Registration)</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>', 'Graphics Card', 0.00, 0.00, NULL, 0, 'products/thumbnails/8LaNj4q5h65whOGAurwMb4rXOsA1zlQaiydemqgQ.jpg', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-07-12 20:14:28', '2026-07-12 20:14:28', 'ZOTAC GeForce GT 1030 Low Profile 2GB GDDR5 Graphics Card', 'ZOTAC GeForce GT 1030 Low Profile 2GB GDDR5 Graphics Card', 'Keywords: Zotac GT 1030 Low Profile price, ZT-P10300A-10L, GeForce GT 1030 2GB GDDR5, NVIDIA Pascal GPU, low profile media center GPU, budget HTPC build Bangladesh', NULL, 141, NULL, NULL),
(1361, 'ZOTAC GAMING GeForce RTX 3050 6GB GDDR6 Solo Graphics Card', 'vThe ZOTAC GAMING GeForce RTX 3050 6GB GDDR6 Solo packs highly efficient 1080p ray-traced gaming and AI acceleration into an ultra-compact, single-fan footprint. Driven by the NVIDIA Ampere architecture, it features a 6GB GDDR6 frame buffer on a 96-bit bus and operates with a highly conservative 70W maximum board consumption. Requiring zero external PCIe power cables and running completely off slot power, its tiny 15 cm length ensures a perfect fit in 99% of desktop PC enclosures—making it the ultimate drop-in upgrade for space-constrained Mini-ITX builds and older pre-built systems.', 'zotac-gaming-geforce-rtx-3050-6gb-gddr6-solo-graphics-card-1783887328', '<p>The <strong>ZOTAC GAMING GeForce RTX 3050 6GB GDDR6 Solo</strong> packs highly efficient 1080p ray-traced gaming and AI acceleration into an ultra-compact, single-fan footprint. Driven by the NVIDIA Ampere architecture, it features a 6GB GDDR6 frame buffer on a 96-bit bus and operates with a highly conservative 70W maximum board consumption. Requiring zero external PCIe power cables and running completely off slot power, its tiny 15 cm length ensures a perfect fit in 99% of desktop PC enclosures—making it the ultimate drop-in upgrade for space-constrained Mini-ITX builds and older pre-built systems.&nbsp;</p>', '<figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Specification Details</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Graphics Processor</td><td>NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 (6GB Variant)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>CUDA Cores</td><td>2,304 Units</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Engine Clock (Boost Mode)</td><td>1470 MHz</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GPU Engine Specs</strong></td><td>Architecture Framework</td><td>NVIDIA Ampere Architecture</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Memory Specs</s